er/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451403} :answer-field/id #uuid "647b263c-7da1-5276-8051-2c582359c8bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19467d2c-d5fe-5bc4-a4cf-8441c5c34caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-47670" :question/problem "Given that a function $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1$, is differentiable at $x=2$, and has a vertical asymptote at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n- **II.** It  is continuous at $x=2$\n- **III.** It is differentiable at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Differentiability implies continuity. Hence,\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$, it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement II is true.   Since $f(x)$ is differentiable at $x=2$ it is also  continuous at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since we have a vertical asymptote at $x=3$, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at this point, hence it can't be differentiable at $x=3$ either."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a48906df-e1ca-5248-b6fb-7970aaafe7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451405} {:answer/id #uuid "f8234ee0-f57e-53fa-b96a-e07bfd2d18fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a48906df-e1ca-5248-b6fb-7970aaafe7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451405} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d19b1ac-9a5a-50ec-a97d-55693e857097" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c132ed2-ebfa-5599-949c-5ab021d1b898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451407} {:answer/id #uuid "2b69fdb0-a788-5959-a521-193c3b4f76ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b69fdb0-a788-5959-a521-193c3b4f76ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451408} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e19491-5a3b-5f58-bca0-720e7aec0cd2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd3a3157-77a5-5d36-87c6-011464c86180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451409} {:answer/id #uuid "d071b426-b3e6-5479-b6bb-4a9d02d85637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d071b426-b3e6-5479-b6bb-4a9d02d85637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451410} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef74da74-37ee-5c81-83e7-fd3dea359ca8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f90e0f73-a650-56a2-851e-2b406e202da6" :question/math-academy-id "q-47679" :question/problem "Given that that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$, has a jump discontinuity at $x=2$, and  is differentiable at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It  is **not** differentiable at $x=2$\n\n- **III.** It is continuous at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x-1|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7586a0dc-25d3-53c5-b3af-cdc314d8fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451411} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc22f55-8ff2-5a8c-bcc3-e6b2be4c1019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7586a0dc-25d3-53c5-b3af-cdc314d8fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451411} :answer-field/id #uuid "f438756f-c79d-53bd-81ac-ca123103d798" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1089274e-1ae2-5b78-a393-34038fd470a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451413} {:answer/id #uuid "501e9e09-32a6-52eb-99c7-4a057e5cb0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "501e9e09-32a6-52eb-99c7-4a057e5cb0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451414} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ec493f-310f-5901-ae51-8ee0e6d54060" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452554} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be1a7df-639d-50cc-ad8c-bbe0418ffddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451415} {:answer/id #uuid "c045dc4a-dc87-5d60-b5ee-eeb1471cb20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6be1a7df-639d-50cc-ad8c-bbe0418ffddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451415} :answer-field/id #uuid "51fbc957-ad59-548f-b7b0-b1fa76bed7e9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8298d153-fa1d-58c6-bfcd-efab6041f9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47681" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+1, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 3, & x=1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **III.** It is differentiable on the interval $(-1,2)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement individually. \n\n- Statement I is false.  At $x=1$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=3,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ ($f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$).\n\n- Statement II is true. Since  $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1,$ it is also not differentiable there (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-1,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7ef1dd-58cc-57f5-9ff9-fc997f4280ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding an Exponential Decay Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048295 :topic/id #uuid "920e0459-5102-56be-8b6e-f637c62f1366" :topic/math-academy-id 1531 :topic/title "Graphing Exponential Decay Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2941b1bd-74eb-50ea-8573-ea6bf303ecbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451417} {:answer/id #uuid "3f4809f8-4607-5abc-b8d1-9148e9780cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2941b1bd-74eb-50ea-8573-ea6bf303ecbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451417} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ef339cd-ca1a-5f68-a181-ddfc41baa3a4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86926aec-34ec-5ca4-a44d-c7e2f64aec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451419} {:answer/id #uuid "3cacd08c-54de-5516-90b4-116e69c23f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86926aec-34ec-5ca4-a44d-c7e2f64aec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451419} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c889f20-b010-5168-b0fc-e32db6413f93" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452557} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a58509-615a-5b66-b885-d2c151888b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451421} {:answer/id #uuid "eed49aff-e179-5980-a3d7-15339409aac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eed49aff-e179-5980-a3d7-15339409aac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451422} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf23fd3-5fce-5331-8251-ee40c271e613" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "182c44b5-94da-5e7b-aa87-a9b6286e7135" :question/math-academy-id "q-47745" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true in relation to the function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Its domain is $x>0$\n- **II.** Its range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty $\n- **III.** It has a horizontal asymptote $y=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=(0.125)^{x}:$\n\n![](images/20/20fae3a813e249a6423567b448a1f5515c3b9127e7c0b82aad541e720db03aca.png)\n\nLet's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ is defined for all input values $x,$ so the domain is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The set of possible outputs of $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ consists of all the positive numbers, so the range is $y>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ increases, the function value gets smaller and smaller, approaching zero. Therefore $y=0$ is a horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x).$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7ef1dd-58cc-57f5-9ff9-fc997f4280ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding an Exponential Decay Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048295 :topic/id #uuid "920e0459-5102-56be-8b6e-f637