ook at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,0]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-1,0]$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,1]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-3,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)^{2}$ is not defined at $x=-2.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a72f0e3-10f9-5627-abc6-e3f1fa8f8634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438314} {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07a11c2-3a82-577e-86eb-fdf2c8fb7f18" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a260fa98-0877-521e-9d9f-d5b6a870fdd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438316} {:answer/id 