wing:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$ and we have $f(-1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, both left-hand side and right-hand side limits exist but they are not the same. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function contains a break exactly at $x=-1$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8e886b-57f2-59c5-b759-e8c984922226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae70a57b-88e6-5264-9484-75fdbfb3d260" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c504c9e2-a62c-527b-a9e7-002c0a5d6492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/valu