e the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1=f(1).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050574 :topic/id #uuid "54ee2cc0-54a0-5d60-a3d0-0b11995e4133" :topic/math-academy-id 462 :topic/title "Determining Continuity from Graphs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482eccea-2346-5593-868b-442a966e9a8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438344} {:answer/id #uuid "8b899347-5cdc-55eb-9237-340f14f06adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b899347-5cdc-55eb-9237-340f14f06adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438345} :answer-field/id #uuid "b283e793-d4da-5d69-a5a1-be0029df36aa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eedcb44f-6a3f-5120-9c70-1dd58a08e127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438346} {:answer/id #uuid "d13de6d5-bfdc-5c50-a6df-fb0dcbf26655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186