id #uuid "b2681d09-12dc-5008-9a96-cf3851901918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439827} {:answer/id #uuid "45d1d269-0f0d-5045-a292-512cf08ada98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2681d09-12dc-5008-9a96-cf3851901918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439827} :answer-field/id #uuid "d271af19-f86b-5002-950a-ed77737b48a3" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "172d7de1-0c8f-50b5-8e69-09efd0164cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-48087" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f53373ebbb7e812471001388ba88122afbde33cd3317c454466168b3e633b58.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$\n- **II.** $x=-2$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=2$\n- **V.** $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "The graph breaks at $x=-2$ and $x=2$ meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-2$ and $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "485fd759-96b3-553f-9eaa-849878c30885" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Jump Discontinuity Given a Function Definition" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050124 :topic/id #uuid "2eb940a7-12ca-5de2-9f75-d2efec304289" :topic/math-academy-id 2003 :topic/title "Jump Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9ffb34-162b-5145-9c40-101a442547a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467608} {:answer/id #uuid "838c1862-e33f-5469-8aaf-7e17990df69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838c1862-e33f-5469-8aaf-7e17990df69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467609} :answer-field/id #uuid "405153bc-6d67-54bd-bd2b-59adea706ce6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573f4b42-cfcf-56d0-9467-f208cd5625a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467610} {:answer/id #uuid "ca467abb-57ef-5f98-bf7e-6827a342e71b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "573f4b42-cfcf-56d0-9467-f208cd5625a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467610} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a64fe7e-2eab-5f3d-93d7-58160ec21920" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88b5c6f6-a2d2-5656-a44f-935d42e30104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467612} {:answer/id #uuid "25356ae2-6276-56b3-8a7d-fffb7a272e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b5c6f6-a2d2-5656-a44f-935d42e30104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467612} :answer-field/id #uuid "016967b9-4c97-5a30-856e-0c57b4dbf834" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93ca2ad1-e9ee-58b8-96fe-892745e095e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-48167" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)$ below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3, & x<1 \\\\ 1-{x}^{3}, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- **II.** It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- **III.** It's continuous at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "For $x=1,$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(1)=1-{1}^{3}=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{2}+3)=({1}^{2}+3)=4\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(1-{x}^{3})=(1-{1}^{3})=0.\n$$\n\nSo both the left and right limits exist and are finite, but they are not equal. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$\n\nHence, I is true, while II and III are false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184220 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Continuity of Two-Piece Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049945 :topic/id #uuid "206244d9-1644-5f25-8714-55d6414eed96" :topic/math-academy-id 3831 :topic/title "Further Continuity of Piecewise Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da5bd1a1-1ca5-5311-b145-0761f9ca6bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451429} {:answer/id #uuid "9a593c2b-218a-5970-95a2-035b3123e586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a593c2b-218a-5970-95a2-035b3123e586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451430} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6fd287-cc3e-5f9b-924b-3e4081c14823" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a066e5eb-ba33-5afa-8b26-913d82960e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451431} {:answer/id #uuid "2d64833f-fd33-5733-8bf9-21c22a441051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d64833f-fd33-5733-8bf9-21c22a441051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451432} :answer-field/id #uuid "42870d10-9c45-5f07-8887-31035d0acee1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452563} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07fbc026-b9f6-5fef-9bda-6578ec268508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451433} {:answer/id #uuid "698d0725-9f21-57bb-81c1-3323aa155dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "698d0725-9f21-57bb-81c1-3323aa155dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451434} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6a04f4-71b0-5572-8590-5bcc64616961" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "764f6881-905e-5e2e-b6a1-fb2e4b876502" :question/math-academy-id "q-48271" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $g(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\begin{aligned}3x-6,\\, & x<1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4,\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=1$\n- **II.** $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=1$\n- **III.** $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $g(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $g(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(1) & ={1}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}g(x) & =3(1)-6 \\\\  & =3-6 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & =g(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=1$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}g(x) & ={1}^{2}-4 \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3 \\\\  & =g(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=1,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048434 :topic/id #uuid "9ef976b2-cf49-59ec-9689-0ec6f4a92d3c" :topic/math-academy-id 288 :topic/title "The Mean Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f17851-b5f1-5589-89e5-4642a8d2d249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467614} {:answer/id #uuid "fe31214d-0432-50de-9cd1-6ad24b62b595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f17851-b5f1-5589-89e5-4642a8d2d249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467614} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1af9b0a-7ec1-5f15-ab7a-56fa74b6fabe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd93754f-1a73-5ffe-8b5e-62295879212b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467616} {:answer/id #uuid "97f0f22d-a1ec-5f03-b20b-292b7ce3521b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f0f22d-a1ec-5f03-b20b-292b7ce3521b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467617} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ff5b55-724a-5d7c-a019-33906583195b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf0a3fa-7f7c-5c54-a84c-1a06af8969ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467618} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed441dd-6085-55e5-843b-f0100f281f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bf0a3fa-7f7c-5c54-a84c-1a06af8969ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467618} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bb492ea-182c-5f4c-80ed-d7362312d50e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12754a03-432b-5bc6-9c26-008364483fd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48497" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4]?$\n- **I.** $g(x)=|x-1|$\n- **II.** $f(x)={x}^{4}$\n- **III.** $h(x)=\\sqrt{x-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4],$ the function must be continuous on $[0,4]$ and differentiable on $(0,4).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)=|x-1|$ is continuous on $[0,4]$ but has a corner at $x=1.$ Hence, it is not differentiable at $x=1,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(0,4).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{4}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[0,4]$ and differentiable on $(0,4).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=\\sqrt{x-1}$ is not defined on $(-\\infty ,1).$ Hence, it is not continuous on $[0,4].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only function II satisfies the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048123 :topic/id #uuid "80ecc4ad-075a-51a6-a1fc-72dc61a2444d" :topic/math-academy-id 313 :topic/title "Global vs. Local Extrema and Critical Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc7d5d6-a451-5962-afc9-9fff555f20ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467620} {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467621} :answer-field/id #uuid "2697fbf1-11b6-59e7-a243-ede0e967f0fe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467622} {:answer/id #uuid "250ef74c-ffc2-556d-a0a3-798c3e88030d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467622} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8df5920-44fd-5cbe-9f0a-2111cda02c34" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} {:answer/id #uuid "762ae4d9-bf4c-5ca6-bb90-84a859083154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2facf3b-7a9b-53cc-9a3f-b2a9bf7a9c24" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "101d0c36-a705-552a-b14b-442022f64eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-48734" :question/problem "![](images/14/14fdc374842064ad40ebbadf3dab16191ecfdeec8c416b4e7f17beffce44fb40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$\n- $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=3.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(3)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement II is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the derivative is undefined at $x=3$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function does not have a local maximum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for $x$ close enough  to the point $x=3,$ so,  actually,  $f(x)$ has local minimum at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048123 :topic/id #uuid "80ecc4ad-075a-51a6-a1fc-72dc61a2444d" :topic/math-academy-id 313 :topic/title "Global vs. Local Extrema and Critical Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1f3def-98d2-524a-b778-f7e66a7f3296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467626} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fbad27-f24f-5ab5-9dc2-2649e548b79d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956e3925-042a-5383-b9cd-d81e8467a088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467628} {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629} :answer-field/id #uuid "98dade12-9621-5587-bfac-2f8ef6ab2b14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b46b1cc-def4-5734-bd89-8f1d5131c333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467630} {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e72066-eadb-5611-801e-ce8cccffd34f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5dfd5ad-23a9-54fc-83bf-a64cab147aed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48737" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a2298a8255a86c803560793658593a22f7f77590ef350c1e0cebd974fce7750.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. $f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$\n\nII. $f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2$ since $f(2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a sharp edge (corner) at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)$ does not exist. Hence, $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, all statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff7c597d-d4a4-5567-add6-eac77475b0d6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Are Neither Local Minima nor Local Maxima" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048478 :topic/id #uuid "a2bb3232-296a-5d16-b145-1ee30beae8b3" :topic/math-academy-id 1360 :topic/title "Using the First Derivative Test to Classify Local Extrema"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35246b30-9622-5ccd-bcb2-7de1b26da85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451435} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0fcb17-1bce-53ec-9825-7b2cb96d89b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35246b30-9622-5ccd-bcb2-7de1b26da85d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451435} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcfdaff-314a-5e47-835a-07070f51bcde" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c49b79f4-6933-5c45-b226-b556b69fd848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451437} {:answer/id #uuid "81a39cfb-34ed-5570-a3ce-a441e908b210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81a39cfb-34ed-5570-a3ce-a441e908b210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451438} :answer-field/id #uuid "6802354d-81af-5fa0-a7f7-e04d14ea15c5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452566} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cff50272-5f7f-5098-8c3a-8221a69e1b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451439} {:answer/id #uuid "4f01cb01-b935-5b64-90c1-4f02f1e90d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cff50272-5f7f-5098-8c3a-8221a69e1b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451439} :answer-field/id #uuid "14e31bb1-d873-56fb-94fe-8650d7568647" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "31bc62dc-b78f-5686-a2a7-468fc236acf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49026" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{e}^{x}},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=0$ is a local maximum\n- **II.** $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum\n- **III.** $x=3$ is a local minimum" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}}{{e}^{x}} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(3-x) & =0 \\\\ x=0,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=0,\\,3.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,4$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =\\frac{3(-1)^{2}-(-1)^{3}}{{e}^{-1}}=4e>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-(1)^{3}}{{e}^{1}}=\\frac{2}{e}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{3(4)^{2}-(4)^{3}}{{e}^{4}}=-\\frac{16}{{e}^{4}}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,3)$ | $3$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $4$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ |  | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=3,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=3$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083303 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1894719c-d398-515d-9a7b-6af74727106c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Improper Integrals of the Second Kind" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050379 :topic/id #uuid "445c7063-c967-5f21-b424-ab8820e310ca" :topic/math-academy-id 759 :topic/title "Improper Integrals of the Second Kind"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d097d65c-ca38-51c7-902f-ceb12ecc4778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467632} {:answer/id #uuid "226a6a50-79b8-5c33-985c-5f775a2757c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "226a6a50-79b8-5c33-985c-5f775a2757c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467633} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b100ce3-ba13-57fa-adb1-8b97906c346c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e91f9305-12b5-5f9a-ad08-1a546a489375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467634} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7cb5b3-dae8-51b6-9737-7ea6e66b57d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e91f9305-12b5-5f9a-ad08-1a546a489375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467634} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf5b4d8f-0e7c-5a34-9eec-fe772d51d84c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e4352e-1743-545b-8868-832df848687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467636} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0cc153-5d01-50ab-9bb3-8a9f885d2be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e4352e-1743-545b-8868-832df848687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467636} :answer-field/id #uuid "24371f23-5748-56a3-bf21-04ee080c6fc5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67f5d543-d28a-5536-ab0c-6f8fec51324b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49928" :question/problem "Which of the following is an improper integral of the second kind?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}-9}\\,$\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}-9}\\,$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I is an improper integral of the second kind since it has finite limits, and \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-9}\\to -\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {3}^{-}.\n$$\n\n- Integral II is an improper integral over an *infinite* domain since its lower limit is infinite.\n\n- Integral III is not an improper integral since it has finite limits and the function under the integral is finite at every point $x\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd82d96b-34d5-5d20-b810-7ea88b0b5797" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048885 :topic/id #uuid "c96ee93a-fd82-595c-824f-e11934066ffc" :topic/math-academy-id 3350 :topic/title "Analyzing Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} {:answer/id #uuid "613a05d1-be2e-50ec-a143-b9bd92523dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} :answer-field/id #uuid "936bcfa4-d2d6-56bc-951a-d3fb63ec7798" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} {:answer/id #uuid "de6a0b4d-d5db-57b2-b79f-fc23d0c4a768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a065266-b7e5-54c1-b994-892844b67807" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} {:answer/id #uuid "3503fafc-99d4-55a2-8b84-ae4563b1ad39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbaebdb6-1441-5c65-a2f2-c74e1d11eb4f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "009c7b44-827f-54c3-aa43-59cb0c58cb71" :question/math-academy-id "q-50143" :question/problem "![](images/50/50472b92dc5fbcc8688bb1d5459f910fb2d3f3c0ee564ba671cb6a53ce8df721.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$\n- ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e3/e328914d55b82fdd07147f683aa44aebbc3f3e908f180e6632332119c81ce482.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the line $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3e3fdc8-67d0-5b46-9c6b-c1ec8d4ea24f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048885 :topic/id #uuid "c96ee93a-fd82-595c-824f-e11934066ffc" :topic/math-academy-id 3350 :topic/title "Analyzing Slope Fields for Nonautonomous Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c66c442f-84ec-5b88-bd98-fd9efdff281b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467644} {:answer/id #uuid "aae2582a-0183-57ed-bc6c-e0fad39e48b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aae2582a-0183-57ed-bc6c-e0fad39e48b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467645} :answer-field/id #uuid "4014543f-2bdb-54cd-b8d4-a799fdbe3913" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58199bae-a5df-50bb-898b-cb09f6da04f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467646} {:answer/id #uuid "edd3e05c-30a9-5909-ad89-48705f604f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58199bae-a5df-50bb-898b-cb09f6da04f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467646} :answer-field/id #uuid "910c1975-2d45-5166-b546-9cc56824291c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb59070-29c0-590f-a938-6111ddb1d321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467648} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddd639c-9761-51b1-bb4e-04dcdf95e6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb59070-29c0-590f-a938-6111ddb1d321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467648} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2598018-4757-537b-839c-45823c668a17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61e999bc-d48d-5bd0-9909-d28a8b568c3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-50349" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a64064f114ac2e6acafa791c4fda50849cad6f3387c4793bdf991c95ae8e542.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x+y$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/6a/6a119b24c773a25bf3530dbfb8574c710cc37a5e970d92112aee5f489551ef02.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $x=0.$\n\n- For $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $y\\to -1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ and for $x\\ne 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{x}{y+1}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x+y$ does not evaluate to zero on $x=0$ (the value depends on $y$).\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ but for $x\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=|\\frac{x}{y-1}|\\to \\frac{|x|}{2}\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050868 :topic/id #uuid "6cc04ddb-ad7b-51e8-8f9d-c71c72f8e9d4" :topic/math-academy-id 684 :topic/title "Convergence of Geometric Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7434f6cd-5abd-5918-983c-90f901173537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467650} {:answer/id #uuid "390198b7-c54f-5cd9-9c6c-20eb14f25176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "390198b7-c54f-5cd9-9c6c-20eb14f25176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467651} :answer-field/id #uuid "9223a194-f14e-5bca-a4c3-a9be1301213f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8c9699-34bd-5a5b-b1d1-7fc0cd00c967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467652} {:answer/id #uuid "32c64784-f8cf-5e6a-8345-7313e29025cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8c9699-34bd-5a5b-b1d1-7fc0cd00c967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467652} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec5739d-20d1-54f9-9ab8-3fc8589202be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0e3c250-5a95-5d66-9b29-c6400da6d824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467654} {:answer/id #uuid "c5386d8a-3465-59f6-895b-f357aefa1a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5386d8a-3465-59f6-895b-f357aefa1a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467655} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f75b307-815b-51f7-b01e-ead1c5a03e0b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29977f9f-fbdd-580d-914b-4f20cb78cbe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-50506" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n- **I.** ${\\sum }_{n=5}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$\n- **II.** ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(2)}^{n}$\n- **III.** ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{8}^{n+1}}{{16}^{n-1}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=5}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ starts with $n=5.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{6}}{{a}_{5}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{6}}{\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(2)}^{n}$ starts with $n=1.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{8{(2)}^{2}}{8{(2)}^{1}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{8}^{n+1}}{{16}^{n-1}}$ starts with $n=0.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{{a}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\frac{{8}^{1+1}}{{16}^{1-1}}}{\\frac{{8}^{0+1}}{{16}^{0-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{{16}^{0}})}{(\\frac{{8}^{1}}{{16}^{-1}})} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{{16}^{0}})(\\frac{{16}^{-1}}{{8}^{1}}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{1})(\\frac{1}{16\\cdot 8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series  I and III converge."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subsets of Special Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050923 :topic/id #uuid "723d1f9c-b696-511c-b5e5-88c045fe7609" :topic/math-academy-id 50 :topic/title "Subsets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce3b13c-fb26-5cdb-823b-ca12d87dcc29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467656} {:answer/id #uuid "4d99d91e-efdd-5a22-8ce6-9d8df760800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d99d91e-efdd-5a22-8ce6-9d8df760800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467657} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f9faab-1148-50bf-98d5-9657cccc6502" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a35154f-b61f-507c-a4f8-90c4cf4d5c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467658} {:answer/id #uuid "9488a339-5ba0-54e0-82a1-c0571ea80c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9488a339-5ba0-54e0-82a1-c0571ea80c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467659} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9e8c14-b0a7-5878-a123-15208210b57a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40a1b98-03b0-592f-9753-c93046815294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467660} {:answer/id #uuid "c964f3a3-9c86-5204-9476-a17284a88218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c964f3a3-9c86-5204-9476-a17284a88218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3695a8e5-9f68-5a86-83e9-3b39972d0070" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe2b18ec-0853-5e8f-951d-8609485c9093" :question/math-academy-id "q-506" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n- **I.** ${Q}^{+}$ (the set of positive rationals)\n- **II.** ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- **III.** $N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every positive rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every negative integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4316287-e6f4-5c71-8743-249965e93785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467662} {:answer/id #uuid "0d5b25f2-ad9a-5e2f-a467-62aebcb4c800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d5b25f2-ad9a-5e2f-a467-62aebcb4c800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467663} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc30e13-6c4c-51bf-9649-4940879f0a6e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15239395-17ec-5d90-8ed6-dae47a5b516c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467664} {:answer/id #uuid "b9279de7-3faf-547d-b961-fdffdf72f3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15239395-17ec-5d90-8ed6-dae47a5b516c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467664} :answer-field/id #uuid "73db372a-04b8-52e1-b15d-153eaeca8010" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812e2132-8055-538a-81b4-e7b919fdc93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467666} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf07043-0394-579e-9adb-f5a8794e6ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "812e2132-8055-538a-81b4-e7b919fdc93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467666} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f7b7695-a3ac-5b03-bf35-127476bb6ba2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3027786-58ab-53d9-9e13-106f7ec40b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-50871" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=0.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=1$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=4$\n- **III.** The series diverges at $x=-2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=0,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[0,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[0,4).$\n\n![](images/a5/a56e24009403f0177f608ba932c03ab77e8db35e1db3e1221c4fb49efca7219f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $1\\in [0,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $4\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-2\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7c7875c-fb08-5fb9-95a6-6d4c334d3a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467668} {:answer/id #uuid "b7697c61-e32a-5449-a404-f95821b2faf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7697c61-e32a-5449-a404-f95821b2faf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467669} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9d32b0-1a92-5c27-a611-84659667e826" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79ed778-e03d-5a13-8aec-70d926886135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467670} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1c2fe6-7bc4-59a9-bd46-db90d677cd88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a79ed778-e03d-5a13-8aec-70d926886135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467670} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb45d0e8-95af-5941-8c8e-1df1bc25a55b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a555f3f3-d734-5304-a0c7-3e541caad244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467672} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5d1cf7-3b8c-5cea-9259-b41ba8e81d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a555f3f3-d734-5304-a0c7-3e541caad244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467672} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c1626a0-6ea2-5f94-b208-8c642c9defd1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2ee1b3ae-f8d2-59d0-abf6-79ccfd75cdf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-50873" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x+2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=-3$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $1,$ i.e., $R\\ge 1.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-3,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-3,-1].$\n\n![](images/93/93ab98aaa7170e5fcef1c090555f259b2030384b6f2f25a282af9d8b6a406ed2.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\in (-3,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-3\\notin (-3,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-\\frac{7}{2}\\notin (-3,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de8e2cbd-2cca-54d4-b53f-11f1742375a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467674} {:answer/id #uuid "90b8c826-ab66-5fe6-9c26-b504e31cd6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de8e2cbd-2cca-54d4-b53f-11f1742375a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467674} :answer-field/id #uuid "47abf491-3b18-517c-9432-1a77835f69ff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c34fdd9-c7d9-5163-8736-d94a57295338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467676} {:answer/id #uuid "228345a5-b436-5fd3-a6b7-477115126239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c34fdd9-c7d9-5163-8736-d94a57295338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467676} :answer-field/id #uuid "79210059-fe37-5b42-ab4d-9e06d408f996" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "603bd9ba-8227-5cfc-ac24-42a89368dbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467678} {:answer/id #uuid "67e22114-28c1-5927-9bf5-6eb1a2a135d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e22114-28c1-5927-9bf5-6eb1a2a135d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467679} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd62b1b3-17ad-588c-b5d5-c422db62c7ea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29a54ff7-5783-54c7-b610-5c600dd04d48" :question/math-academy-id "q-50874" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-4,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series diverges at $x=-5$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=2$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-4,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-4,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-4,2).$ \n\n![](images/a2/a246a6460d15037b469072b4275e51ff4dd9c56242f6ffeae1bebc2adf66f39f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $2\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $-3\\in [-4,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2300bae0-298d-53b8-ab0d-12d87ac46d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467680} {:answer/id #uuid "36bc1938-4be5-5a3d-aa29-252dd524ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36bc1938-4be5-5a3d-aa29-252dd524ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467681} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceabd937-f087-5722-8c9a-d4dbf4d0f9b4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e39a0cb-6e4d-56d5-a23c-41c3a5e61762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467682} {:answer/id #uuid "0b2ffdc0-c8c8-569e-89da-2c6ea8c2aea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e39a0cb-6e4d-56d5-a23c-41c3a5e61762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467682} :answer-field/id #uuid "9426409a-ac6f-506c-98a7-5f83162b0a11" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf5703cc-2efe-559c-9fb5-ff676ba60b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467684} {:answer/id #uuid "04771c22-bce4-501c-a4b9-4f52d83ab3ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf5703cc-2efe-559c-9fb5-ff676ba60b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467684} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bfba346-6758-55bf-9798-0053f1e86ced" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32c4dcc9-1fba-5e61-8a0a-ad46399f9d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-50876" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{5}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{5}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$\n\n![](images/57/57208948dece1112674d3578763bc8d6b73d1d6ab91d160b14839e16a39cf2f6.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $-3\\in (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{7}{2}\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f76e57a-1ca0-528a-83d8-a658b709ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answ