} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467690} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccae151c-97cd-5e93-9baa-a5d477ca5334" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0bcb862b-db75-545a-8402-c194bc3da35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50877" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-2.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=1$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=8$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $5,$ i.e., $R\\ge 5.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-2,8).$\n\n![](images/38/38763aa0d87065a01ccdf0d94bca2a4e1d6ef227aeab4aaacb9703246eee6abf.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-3\\notin [-2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $1\\in [-2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $8\\notin [-2,8),$  we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements must be true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6e5e228-fa65-531d-a8da-e444079bd9d8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Series Using Multiple Convergence Tests" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050498 :topic/id #uuid "4e0180b3-521f-51e5-843f-0f6c55fd18f7" :topic/math-academy-id 1172 :topic/title "Selecting Procedures for Analyzing Infinite Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "624b7117-00f8-551a-809e-5d1c3ff1debc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467692} {:answer/id #uuid "a1161ac7-f2a2-58a6-8a07-6b82fbac85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1161ac7-f2a2-58a6-8a07-6b82fbac85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467693} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b52ba51-dd6a-5109-ad4a-86c7ab07785f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468567} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a95e3e6-c21e-5dba-88b4-2aa448e29ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467694} {:answer/id #uuid "c80a45eb-af40-56af-be7f-df024e54b91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a95e3e6-c21e-5dba-88b4-2aa448e29ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467694} :answer-field/id #uuid "640dfa81-f2e1-5fca-a3e6-abf23e497d33" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52924de1-0701-5aac-9b3a-e34d33354697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467696} {:answer/id #uuid "dde7684e-a4ef-50e4-a409-ed9aeefc8f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52924de1-0701-5aac-9b3a-e34d33354697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467696} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a21870-3114-52a9-bdfe-348f688b5b7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a500c68-ffb3-5162-a19f-22fd0f314af1" :question/math-academy-id "q-50971" :question/problem "Which of the following series converge?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}$\n\nIII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We use the flowchart below to determine which tests to use for each series.\n\n![](images/3a/3aa7f0243efeab51d00aa9694dd018245f7ca4664cc1a5fdf4e646aebb61536e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's test each series in turn.\n\n- For the first series, we use the alternating series test. Observe that \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n!}\n$$\n\nis positive and decreasing for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, by the alternating series test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}\n$$\n\nis also convergent.\n\n- For the second series, we use the limit comparison test. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nWorking out the necessary limit, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{b}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}÷\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\cdot \\sqrt{n}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2n}{n+2}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2}{(1+\\frac{2}{n})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $L=2$ is positive and finite. Now, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nis divergent by the $p$-series test. So, the series \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\n$$\n\nis also divergent by the limit comparison test.\n\n- For the final series, we use the $n$th term test for divergence. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThen, we have ${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\infty ,$ since the polynomial in the numerator grows faster than the polynomial in the denominator. Therefore, by the $n$th term test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nis divergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only series I converges." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420497} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420537} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/title "Mathematical Methods for the Physical Sciences II: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545198} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545907}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115382 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a4f6c8-31fa-50e6-8924-9043f086fc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451441} {:answer/id #uuid "17996804-872e-51f5-a6c0-71ff10f790c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06a4f6c8-31fa-50e6-8924-9043f086fc71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451441} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e5b6922-7038-562e-a4b1-61d0975cf86e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba3df986-ffe9-5d03-8865-ce74fde6c5fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451443} {:answer/id #uuid "70ec42d9-18ea-5a54-9ad6-5d9d94f65f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ec42d9-18ea-5a54-9ad6-5d9d94f65f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451444} :answer-field/id #uuid "af457962-dc41-51fd-9da3-30f0f5721ea6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbbbf598-0a23-5bc8-bc07-1db35acde805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451445} {:answer/id #uuid "610fe76c-881c-5006-8df1-8049eab6fe4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "610fe76c-881c-5006-8df1-8049eab6fe4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451446} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ec4e02-a297-5c90-a788-b2d6829328af" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "227ca0fe-b4ce-570a-82ea-2de7f8f95c49" :question/math-academy-id "q-51067" :question/problem "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$, has a cusp at $x=1,$ and is differentiable at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is differentiable at $x=-2$\n\n- **II.** It's **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **III.** ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=f(3).$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x+2|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a cusp at $x=1$, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is true. Differentiability implies continuity. Hence, ${lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=f(3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5633afc7-e223-5130-9090-0d9865542257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467698} {:answer/id #uuid "8be09054-e939-5cc8-b92f-f214cfcf82fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be09054-e939-5cc8-b92f-f214cfcf82fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467699} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1f48bc-fb36-5f83-8aa7-46fb5cb2d82e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d41b96c3-cfe1-58c9-a62b-16aa45f88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467700} {:answer/id #uuid "87a1ad38-a41b-5686-a7ca-5d675ff2cf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d41b96c3-cfe1-58c9-a62b-16aa45f88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467700} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d22340-4fa0-5014-8865-2d0be6f7f86d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ed64b73-5791-59b1-83e8-1e3d847f7927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467702} {:answer/id #uuid "d539c28a-0e2c-5ae6-8fef-98fd25e1625a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ed64b73-5791-59b1-83e8-1e3d847f7927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467702} :answer-field/id #uuid "0523546d-7928-515a-b054-7e46e591c14b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc8d31c1-2a52-5465-9bb5-91b8bdc2abf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51070" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5eae80c03e35f79eaa484a5d54f7fa1a0ec46a5f27480fb69089efab938eba06.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $f(x)$ has a cusp at this point and so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ and so it is not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e9e5a96-4534-58ea-bab8-06e75a58241f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451447} {:answer/id #uuid "37186cca-00e9-556e-9ebb-cf5c0f3d22fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e9e5a96-4534-58ea-bab8-06e75a58241f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451447} :answer-field/id #uuid "a759576c-6748-54ed-b630-631dd1491276" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c9d7f40-ce2a-5069-b244-f2015404fbec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451449} {:answer/id #uuid "dca9b7a5-d530-5de9-88ae-c75a211f007e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c9d7f40-ce2a-5069-b244-f2015404fbec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451449} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ffd2573-bf93-588a-948e-63534ae3550a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc1ab0af-7df7-5290-9161-a4b21fba48ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451451} {:answer/id #uuid "585c3f02-a77d-56b4-9200-a30714a42bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "585c3f02-a77d-56b4-9200-a30714a42bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451452} :answer-field/id #uuid "385e7e32-dae1-552f-b1b3-a83635627292" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ce07619-7707-5d93-86b3-865c0def2d71" :question/math-academy-id "q-51072" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4, & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ x+2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It is differentiable on the interval $(-2,2)$\n\n- **III.** It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false and statement III is true. Indeed,  let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, $x=1.$ At this point, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(-x+4)=-1+4=3 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(x+2)=1+2=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ (it has a removable discontinuity there). Hence, it is also not differentiable at this point.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-2,2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092329 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a0cc5ea-7f70-5c5f-841e-01a6813da8c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Operations on Polynomials" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049755 :topic/id #uuid "1125135d-4341-5e5d-9065-381cc0460203" :topic/math-academy-id 942 :topic/title "Closure Properties of Polynomials"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77424b74-59a9-5c2e-89f0-53f435b5033d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451453} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1279d2-3147-5295-841a-4ce24090acc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77424b74-59a9-5c2e-89f0-53f435b5033d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451453} :answer-field/id #uuid "c548a60a-c199-5729-895f-34b3e5f45a36" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095c6424-f1c4-5d05-8776-6ddbd7b4fc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451455} {:answer/id #uuid "c835045e-9782-52ec-a10f-b277f56f6df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "095c6424-f1c4-5d05-8776-6ddbd7b4fc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451455} :answer-field/id #uuid "a403ccc9-5fbe-5966-b84a-1177104148a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e64965b8-1c7e-5430-bf58-d6a52cb11bf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451457} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1b4f3d-a4de-5ffa-955e-62cb4945a9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e1b4f3d-a4de-5ffa-955e-62cb4945a9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451458} :answer-field/id #uuid "876b12da-85bd-58c3-986f-93368746b2ed" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12650667-2b8f-5503-bd94-74dd3c8919fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-51690" :question/problem "Given that $P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $3,$ which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3{x}^{3}-P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $3$\n- **II.** $3{x}^{3}+P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $3$\n- **III.** $3{x}^{3}\\cdot P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $6$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, suppose $P=3{x}^{3}-1.$ Then $3{x}^{3}-P(x)=3{x}^{3}-(3{x}^{3}-1)=1,$ which is not a polynomial of degree $3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, suppose $P=-3{x}^{3}.$ Then $3{x}^{3}+P(x)=3{x}^{3}+(-3{x}^{3})=0,$ which is not a polynomial of degree $3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The highest-degree term in $P$ must contain ${x}^{3}.$ Therefore, the highest-degree term in $3{x}^{3}\\cdot P(x)$ must contain ${x}^{3}\\cdot {x}^{3}={x}^{3+3}={x}^{6},$ meaning that $3{x}^{3}\\cdot P(x)$ has degree $6.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147430 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Simple Harmonic Motion Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050824 :topic/id #uuid "69970c4c-efa5-537d-a31c-79a56da6e61a" :topic/math-academy-id 2524 :topic/title "Simple Harmonic Oscillators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c1f2c3b-1d34-5c06-b61c-46d1903e5e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467704} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dcd9f-31c4-523b-8ddc-4637dfa9e777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dcd9f-31c4-523b-8ddc-4637dfa9e777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467705} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb0f775-1530-52d1-b49f-df3b6017042f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468573} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1598357d-613f-5fc5-8ce1-55e7dc1b98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467706} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0b795c-450c-5317-b8c4-dcb8c540442b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1598357d-613f-5fc5-8ce1-55e7dc1b98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467706} :answer-field/id #uuid "38477ec7-e808-5dbf-9eda-11186731007f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ab47045-d431-52de-91f8-aac2544bdf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467708} {:answer/id #uuid "099ed570-a048-5749-af1f-b679324dbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "099ed570-a048-5749-af1f-b679324dbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467709} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f979ad1-f9a7-5092-b7cc-ebe822b551bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "347ed2fe-a388-536f-85e7-6e55844b3b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-64252" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n- **I.** $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n- **II.** $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n- **III.** $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=81\\,⟹\\,\\omega =9.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t$\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III could be used to represent $y(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147432 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a459ec25-988e-5f91-8c25-2b7b81b6b6ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of a Mass-Spring System" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050824 :topic/id #uuid "69970c4c-efa5-537d-a31c-79a56da6e61a" :topic/math-academy-id 2524 :topic/title "Simple Harmonic Oscillators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ae52197-a20b-5e41-8512-ade86a30a251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451459} {:answer/id #uuid "5e89b216-7e69-5a8f-afc3-37363604f2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e89b216-7e69-5a8f-afc3-37363604f2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451460} :answer-field/id #uuid "18027867-876c-5faf-b00e-b73b20c5256a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5a51e83-a567-584f-8e17-72bb72d73b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451461} {:answer/id #uuid "71b8ee3a-1486-598b-a83d-7074d88bd021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71b8ee3a-1486-598b-a83d-7074d88bd021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451462} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7cc036f-bb50-545c-bf8d-b6e00789748a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd78168c-f998-58a4-a370-22b3e328ef26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451463} {:answer/id #uuid "80215a01-c856-568e-96cb-ab6d4c25fc14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd78168c-f998-58a4-a370-22b3e328ef26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451463} :answer-field/id #uuid "8668e3d0-dc33-53f0-9415-719e6bc43716" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "260eecb9-d0fb-5697-b47b-f5982b239650" :question/math-academy-id "q-64258" :question/problem "A particle of mass $32\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=8\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$ The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds. \n\nIf the particle moves with simple harmonic motion, then which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The governing differential equation is ${y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0$\n- **II.** The frequency $f$ of the oscillation is $f=\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}$\n- **III.** The general solution can be expressed as $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{4}+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{4}$ where $R$ is the amplitude and $ϕ$ is the phase." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with simple harmonic motion (SHM) under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above equation gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{k}{m}y=0.\n$$\n\nComparing this to the SHM equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe see that\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{k}{m}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $k$ and $m$ gives\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{8}{32}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSo the governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0.\n$$\n\nHence, statement I is true.\n\n- The frequency $f$ (measured in ${s}^{-1}$) is given by\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{1}{T}=\\frac{\\omega }{2\\pi },\n$$\n\nwhere $T$ is the period. So in our case, we have\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2\\pi }=\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\,.\n$$\n\nSo the frequency $f=\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\nHence, statement II is true.\n\n- The general solution for $y(t)$ can take one of three forms.\n\n- $A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\n- $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\nWriting $\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}$ in form 1 gives\n\n$$\ny(t)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, statement III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "089c1139-6e3a-5240-be03-fb7e54ecbd7c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Types of Damped Oscillations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048291 :topic/id #uuid "91890390-2801-5fd4-8f87-a9c37f742926" :topic/math-academy-id 2525 :topic/title "Damped Oscillators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f631397-1fc5-5f73-8f1c-6752ba962aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451465} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd4b1af-69f4-5724-900e-69d4836fcf5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdd4b1af-69f4-5724-900e-69d4836fcf5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451466} :answer-field/id #uuid "6374e92f-3ad0-501c-9e81-fde082964406" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fca6602-54be-566a-94ca-51a24f960139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451467} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef9320d-e4ac-5a81-bcca-b06cac9ffce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fca6602-54be-566a-94ca-51a24f960139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451467} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4230243-b999-5225-8057-f0e153de4518" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7875532-f5c7-5be9-bb70-9565d2e57d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451469} {:answer/id #uuid "10d8e653-fcc4-5468-9d5b-1c81e9786209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7875532-f5c7-5be9-bb70-9565d2e57d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451469} :answer-field/id #uuid "b08c2525-28fa-502f-a408-27b29f00cddd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dca080f-586e-56e2-9297-7dcd4b704b21" :question/math-academy-id "q-64615" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping.\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping." :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+8y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +8=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(8) & =-16<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents light damping, and so statement I is correct.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+6{y}^{′}+9y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={6}^{2}-4(1)(9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement II is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={3}^{2}-4(1)(2) & =1>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048291 :topic/id #uuid "91890390-2801-5fd4-8f87-a9c37f742926" :topic/math-academy-id 2525 :topic/title "Damped Oscillators"} :activity/title "Damped Oscillators" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492219} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492983}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "089c1139-6e3a-5240-be03-fb7e54ecbd7c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Types of Damped Oscillations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048291 :topic/id #uuid "91890390-2801-5fd4-8f87-a9c37f742926" :topic/math-academy-id 2525 :topic/title "Damped Oscillators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4d59c3e-75ce-51a7-8f80-30093ac25485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451471} {:answer/id #uuid "df3809da-1961-51c2-befc-f97475589202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d59c3e-75ce-51a7-8f80-30093ac25485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451471} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae86ba8c-3bab-523a-8d68-5f2352daa2cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f9f4a53-2943-5d8d-8aa8-5c7c7b820119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451473} {:answer/id #uuid "e942a680-194a-56cb-9d78-a58b9e4917ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f9f4a53-2943-5d8d-8aa8-5c7c7b820119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451473} :answer-field/id #uuid "8edd13b2-454e-51aa-aa76-1674abdd5f7f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f06fc11-aedb-57cf-835d-c18570ffedec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451475} {:answer/id #uuid "9eab41cd-d5aa-56dc-8a6d-81d4d83fd5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eab41cd-d5aa-56dc-8a6d-81d4d83fd5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451476} :answer-field/id #uuid "30721295-a83c-5127-bc4e-ad272fe63ebf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452585}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c1c35ed-7049-53ec-934c-7b92d30ad741" :question/math-academy-id "q-64616" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing critical damping.\n\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing light damping.\n\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents an oscillator undergoing heavy damping." :question/worked-solution "Remember that, given the equation of a damped harmonic oscillator, the type of damping depends on the discriminant of the characteristic equation:\n\n- $D>0$ leads to heavy damping,\n\n- $D=0$ leads to critical damping, and\n\n- $D<0$ leads to light damping.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each equation.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +6=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={5}^{2}-4(1)(6) & =1>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement I is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={2}^{2}-4(1)(1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement II is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +2=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(2) & =8>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement III is correct.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050677 :topic/id #uuid "5e132315-9606-5b30-bee3-61f0209d40c4" :topic/math-academy-id 2548 :topic/title "Introduction to Second-Order Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e735dc0-c691-579e-b252-edb026eeb71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467710} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d75e2e-d6bc-57ec-ae37-c69815c776ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1d75e2e-d6bc-57ec-ae37-c69815c776ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467711} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c70e2c6-e1e0-5572-9a05-ea0878c65ffa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a16d1d62-6621-503c-b0f9-bb715a8e1719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467712} {:answer/id #uuid "8440d621-4497-5133-9c62-17940a40a383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a16d1d62-6621-503c-b0f9-bb715a8e1719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467712} :answer-field/id #uuid "5635e07f-ff2a-5127-b631-682d05273e69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302cc8e5-06fe-55a0-88f7-cec7955d38ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467714} {:answer/id #uuid "6eded924-e650-5770-8da5-7d37948d90ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302cc8e5-06fe-55a0-88f7-cec7955d38ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467714} :answer-field/id #uuid "4603a9a6-bdb5-51e4-b71c-7872c6351545" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bb9654d-ae6a-57d3-8c11-b8ef9be232d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65009" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- **III.** $3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $4{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "101e0c22-fbb4-5865-af5f-d669e2488d09" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Linear ODEs Using the Superposition Principle" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050032 :topic/id #uuid "277bf882-73ab-515e-84e5-4f7920acb235" :topic/math-academy-id 2549 :topic/title "The Superposition Principle"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e3999b2-cf3e-53ba-b81a-57a1167c43cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467716} {:answer/id #uuid "e76b57b4-95b4-56db-80ee-bc842c04362e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e3999b2-cf3e-53ba-b81a-57a1167c43cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467716} :answer-field/id #uuid "520b20a9-67a9-510c-8a4a-bf10f927a343" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ba558e-45ea-593a-af35-72261d300bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467718} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ab3a22-dcda-5034-a911-7a04245aaa46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8ab3a22-dcda-5034-a911-7a04245aaa46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467719} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d2cd27b-8211-54d2-9058-e0c068b1afab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ae1854-407d-5cdf-9e7f-245569682d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467720} {:answer/id #uuid "711403d4-4ed8-57e7-8ea2-e5ed05de59dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ae1854-407d-5cdf-9e7f-245569682d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467720} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ad8c85-9200-5cf3-89f3-a6b9e7622899" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7815e919-91eb-5d8d-8ac9-3683413b2268" :question/math-academy-id "q-65110" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}+4y=0,$ which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}$\n- **II.** $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- **III.** $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ are constants, then $y(x)={c}_{1}{y}_{1}(x)+{c}_{2}{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nWe're given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Therefore, the following function is also a solution:\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}$ is **not** a solution of the given equation. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotient of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is a solution of the given equation. Here, ${c}_{1}=1,{c}_{2}=5.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is **not** a solution of the given equation because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is not a solution."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29610715-333d-5e0c-9328-eec1d45f56ed" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Limits Along Different Paths for Multivariable Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048449 :topic/id #uuid "a05758d1-f2b4-5a86-b7b0-c2a4bb6dcb85" :topic/math-academy-id 1931 :topic/title "Limits and Continuity of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f09aafd-c1e5-5dd1-bf03-b73681599bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451477} {:answer/id #uuid "2f54d447-a39c-55bb-850f-c236243803eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f09aafd-c1e5-5dd1-bf03-b73681599bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451477} :answer-field/id #uuid "85c75200-01ed-54ca-9326-1eca1bb956f5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf599bcb-83ed-5f4a-a06d-a9db97c5fe77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451479} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec1810-7d26-56cd-aaac-4334475ae5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec1810-7d26-56cd-aaac-4334475ae5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451480} :answer-field/id #uuid "a87ea30f-e244-5f86-bffc-4a5395ff286d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca681fe9-ee18-536a-9299-af74510e99ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451481} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5393a0-13ec-5e60-9584-47126e03236e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca681fe9-ee18-536a-9299-af74510e99ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451481} :answer-field/id #uuid "118478a6-d6eb-5b08-b5c7-fcce661c9509" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ccd0f4b9-0dbd-51e2-a95c-14471c65ba52" :question/math-academy-id "q-65145" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{2y+x}{3x+y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$\n\n- **II.** The limit evaluates to $-\\frac{1}{2}$ along the path $y=-x$\n\n- **III.** The limit exists and is equal to $0$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{2y+x}{3x+y}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0+0}{3\\cdot 0+0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\frac{2y+x}{3x+y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x+x}{3x+x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x}{4x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-x}\\frac{2y+x}{3x+y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-2x+x}{3x-x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-x}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{2y+x}{3x+y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c4f7c1-2cc1-57ed-a18b-bf91992e00d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451483} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e4c2de-8568-5ff2-baf8-40d15c25b5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3e4c2de-8568-5ff2-baf8-40d15c25b5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451484} :answer-field/id #uuid "99c60c75-d597-5852-8b29-5420ba46e80b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96e8d67b-c006-521e-ad4e-1b3b5e5bbae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451485} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcff0a4-c6d8-5ff7-9344-ecba3634e8b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e8d67b-c006-521e-ad4e-1b3b5e5bbae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451485} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf8a887b-1bb0-5b36-af98-54f46b4ff833" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd09d87-8f09-5958-88e2-49043d0205b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451487} {:answer/id #uuid "72089ef2-d948-531c-b1f3-ac84e9dc1b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72089ef2-d948-531c-b1f3-ac84e9dc1b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451488} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4fe7e1-7135-5cca-a3a0-20d39be1b879" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b22bd39f-49d5-56c7-8797-705e83876e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-65255" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=xy{e}^{x/y}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}_{x}(0,1)$is defined\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{y}(1,0)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{x/y}) \\\\  & =y{e}^{x/y}+xy{e}^{x/y}(\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =y{e}^{x/y}+x{e}^{x/y} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{x/y}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{x/y}+xy{e}^{x/y}(-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{x/y}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}{e}^{x/y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(0,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(0,1)=0\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{0/1}=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,1)=1\\cdot {e}^{0/1}+0\\cdot {e}^{0/1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. If we substitute $(1,0)$ into ${f}_{y}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{y}(1,0)=1\\cdot {e}^{1/0}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{0}\\cdot {e}^{1/0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(1,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,1)=1\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{1/1}=e,\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,1) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1/1}+1\\cdot {e}^{1/1}=2e \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,1) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1/1}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{1}\\cdot {e}^{1/1}=e-e=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409538} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409562}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049991 :topic/id #uuid "245d7b8c-ac58-53e1-bbb6-af3096067f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3567 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosecant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e211abea-7b27-5a54-be2b-2776b824b945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438350} {:answer/id #uuid "79899ac4-ccf6-540e-b658-cb8b94ac43da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e211abea-7b27-5a54-be2b-2776b824b945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438350} :answer-field/id #uuid "edae0a14-27e5-5e98-b83b-4156e2b25186" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67a95286-58a4-575f-9e02-1c66187d6d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438352} {:answer/id #uuid "eea5daa5-e442-5597-9cec-3ad2abc796cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67a95286-58a4-575f-9e02-1c66187d6d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438352} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf74774a-d3c3-5b92-9271-5390bf41b92d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2548a6ab-0a8e-5889-96af-63d49ce1229d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438354} {:answer/id #uuid "f0494e1c-1e6b-50ae-bba0-b1f997d7bb40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0494e1c-1e6b-50ae-bba0-b1f997d7bb40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438355} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ca7e1ae-07e6-57e8-afc7-3d171793c761" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7573ddef-f834-5ca7-911d-588bad3a2d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-65307" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049991 :topic/id #uuid "245d7b8c-ac58-53e1-bbb6-af3096067f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3567 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosecant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f89c4d-da0d-58fc-ab37-efc5ed7f1053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} :answer-field/id #uuid "30435fb6-1037-57a8-b967-d652cdf699a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ebde88-a46b-560f-9b2d-c9311641fa24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438358} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa49081-1dec-5a36-ad7e-37cc67073211" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} {:answer/id #uuid "d95548b2-40ec-5ebf-b1ab-d29936ab04f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} :answer-field/id #uuid "168eb318-5e34-58b3-8153-3564c073e9ff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69d68c82-75d2-569e-bc5a-a35be8a71a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050359 :topic/id #uuid "424e5d7e-179f-525e-bdaa-70125807f572" :topic/math-academy-id 3563 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e69034ac-dafa-5930-9534-071e532133a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451489} {:answer/id #uuid "c79d71f8-411a-5d53-9c3b-a808ff276fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69034ac-dafa-5930-9534-071e532133a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451489} :answer-field/id #uuid "af683c1c-fb93-51f7-8ac5-a2a162727948" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aefb0cc-b61a-591b-938a-61ea84ad8322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451491} {:answer/id #uuid "94538785-9bb8-5d4c-adcd-8998ecf59214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aefb0cc-b61a-591b-938a-61ea84ad8322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451491} :answer-field/id #uuid "140a5ba5-395f-5a59-8c85-ed4334f12df7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452593} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb55f19f-2e84-5c66-b274-dd496fc42c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451493} {:answer/id #uuid "e78d352f-70a9-5fb3-9cb7-e1d6d348d4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78d352f-70a9-5fb3-9cb7-e1d6d348d4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451494} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01f97a5-285a-5298-bb3d-ba1bb2236b16" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e763b192-f670-5ee9-881f-7ff2a2620e1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-65332" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-\\pi $ is not in the domain of the function. $$\n- **II.** $y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is in the range of the function. $$\n- **III.** $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is defined for $x=-\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is not in the range.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $, thus $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba108ea-f332-5102-ab91-06fceec4d251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d3662e-e09c-5f64-98c3-e20f9b22d088" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9529cf39-39ef-5312-a424-5a724c472342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467724} {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725} :answer-field/id #uuid "211c78a3-c7f3-5811-864c-a8d524c6218e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "269da86c-2941-58e2-a59d-268c780b46cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467726} {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b3e117-4a2a-5afd-8320-ffa1d5324c25" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75bb764-05ea-55ac-922e-cca49efb6283" :question/math-academy-id "q-65821" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(0,-2\\pi )$\n- **II.** $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- **III.** $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(0,-2\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-2\\pi ,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-2\\pi $ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,-2\\pi )$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8f2dda-cd81-5f6e-b768-a55c41ebc669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467728} {:answer/id #uuid "9734881e-341a-559d-9cd7-c83cf09900eb" :answer/ty