nswer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d73755a9-64c2-5f37-ae61-9ec0e51a1fdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467756} {:answer/id #uuid "4243e1e1-006d-51f1-85b7-ab436fce1d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4243e1e1-006d-51f1-85b7-ab436fce1d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467757} :answer-field/id #uuid "53e70ba6-6ea7-557f-b8f1-3d7ee5384d35" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "170337cb-28d4-5a79-b92e-2d074da465f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-66007" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n- **I.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=11\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-10$\n- **III.** $3\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-1$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=1$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{4}$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation III has no solutions."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:d