:db/id #edb/ref 17592186439269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1a88c7-0f27-56c5-b163-10cc23842fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438482} {:answer/id #uuid "97a592ec-ef1e-56af-8795-1ae139a9168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97a592ec-ef1e-56af-8795-1ae139a9168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438483} :answer-field/id #uuid "92e3b518-970c-5ddb-8ddd-c289c427c026" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "924829bc-4eac-54c3-82c8-f773955ca97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-69834" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $M$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $det(M)=1$\n- **III.** $det(M)=0$\n\n \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-4-12)+2(-2+6)+1(4+4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-16)+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =-16+8+8 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050191 :topic/id #uuid "35093636-213e-50dc-8f50-148c780d5517" :topic/math-academy-id 157 :topic/title "The Complex Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d614e154-522b-544f-8e9c-386df0d0c800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467794} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae5580b-7c4f-5ba3-bb0b-eb3c703d1870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ae5580b-7c4f-5ba3-bb0b-eb3c703d1870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467795} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61d5bd6-46a4-5cd0-aa62-aa2d0ced7d24" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468618} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f065ca-983e-5c46-90fd-f0019d09f69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467796} {:answer/id #uuid "93e6b5cb-aa60-5568-abc2-92f2b5428216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7f065ca-983e-5c46-90fd-f0019d09f69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467796} :answer-field/id #uuid "05074ec7-d5e0-5eba-8a67-483c4409e9cf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcd7aed7-0d0e-529e-8d09-ecde7c5392d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467798} {:answer/id #uuid "33fb7d2a-63d2-52e4-ac91-b5b2eed80714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33fb7d2a-63d2-52e4-ac91-b5b2eed80714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467799} :answer-field/id #uuid "166b7ba0-0bab-5589-8707-f329fc4be250" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "36192a12-3447-5ff2-9e37-3b54bb995a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-69899" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the second quadrant in an Argand diagram?\n- **I.** $-2+\\text{i}$\n- **II.** $-3-2\\text{i}$\n- **III.** $-3+2\\text{i}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $-2+\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,1)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,-2)$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-3+2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-3$ and the imaginary part $y=2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-3,2)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n![](images/d6/d683b808bee4b7893952adbaf87940066f9ff7d61c99ce7cc7e05fc9a4fbe02f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6a3d254-c96f-5aa0-9db6-a587eb7cb2de" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Expression Involving Given Determinants and Matrix Types" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049159 :topic/id #uuid "df2bac79-2def-521c-b3f0-baba942d57fa" :topic/math-academy-id 1771 :topic/title "Basic Properties of Determinants"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e580d0f-e9fe-5941-a12f-c8763dc11a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451495} {:answer/id #uuid "4cb18a3b-644d-5457-8074-4bd65a0f98ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cb18a3b-644d-5457-8074-4bd65a0f98ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451496} :answer-field/id #uuid "14e31e65-2e80-5d33-b122-e9f49c484a5b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab46de1a-5553-5082-894a-18b3d641e4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451497} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1be7de-5296-5de8-8b84-a5bc2004eae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab46de1a-5553-5082-894a-18b3d641e4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451497} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea670fc-e390-5d6c-ae3f-e46fb09b3a8b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f62f59e-826f-5cc6-8775-8d4e0f0d3d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451499} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1689ff-de50-5771-9def-c85576354e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab1689ff-de50-5771-9def-c85576354e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451500} :answer-field/id #uuid "09736dae-a711-5cd2-973a-5998a4c4ecee" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "029d7f47-3f9c-597a-ac75-8fbf40dc3193" :question/math-academy-id "q-70105" :question/problem "Given that $det({A}^{T})=8$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=0$\n- **II.** $2\\text{det}(A)+\\text{det}(I)=16$\n- **III.** $3\\text{det}(I)-2\\text{det}(A)=-13$" :question/worked-solution "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)=\\text{det}({A}^{T})=8\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=8-8=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n2\\text{det}(A)+\\text{det}(I)=2\\cdot 8+1=17\\ne 16.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\text{det}(I)-2\\text{det}(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 8=-13.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050129 :topic/id #uuid "2eee4710-3f26-5186-948b-a819cfaf4083" :topic/math-academy-id 1775 :topic/title "Cramer's Rule for 2x2 Systems of Linear Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae2925c-3b96-520c-a0d3-abd31d1b1a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467800} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c35df2-2bc6-5aff-a8c0-5983afd08cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ae2925c-3b96-520c-a0d3-abd31d1b1a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467800} :answer-field/id #uuid "9964608f-6d33-5d23-ad89-67c51daca483" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51e75d4-d650-5dde-bab9-f44d9ed0ba19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467802} {:answer/id #uuid "2ddc6cc2-a2f6-5c31-89bf-5e97f4160d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f51e75d4-d650-5dde-bab9-f44d9ed0ba19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467802} :answer-field/id #uuid "21a74bb3-8d72-54f1-aaee-8348f893cc5c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554d0d1b-860a-576b-b335-77efc0624d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467804} {:answer/id #uuid "4374345d-6d8f-5041-923b-26fb3a674b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4374345d-6d8f-5041-923b-26fb3a674b3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467805} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ccbcc4-dfe8-569e-8534-c9a02b85e5b8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e21820bb-bc15-5fe3-a578-6f44daf46f1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70252" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky &=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338799 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091 :topic/id #uuid "d9b41e19-22fc-5fad-93ae-b8f50010d70b" :topic/math-academy-id 3557 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7fc3c01-7f3a-5c6b-abd7-c743ce206e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438490} {:answer/id #uuid "47099553-c6c1-5bd1-9e0e-9f21c98fc65f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7fc3c01-7f3a-5c6b-abd7-c743ce206e9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438490} :answer-field/id #uuid "a81ed0d9-7e42-5cbb-aca1-b03bc48b3022" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46870e8a-9f05-53d2-a4ea-6c68291e1467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438492} {:answer/id #uuid "71ec84ae-38af-5df8-81fd-d23b40330600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71ec84ae-38af-5df8-81fd-d23b40330600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438493} :answer-field/id #uuid "faf0da50-2691-505e-8eef-7d1db6e3c6e2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550bb9f1-5049-57d7-84d3-41f3f2ac8184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438494} {:answer/id #uuid "a91fa62b-3e27-5516-b774-e6cf906a51d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "550bb9f1-5049-57d7-84d3-41f3f2ac8184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438494} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5214bf9-b022-5d37-a8e8-c3abbfca85a8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5773d37-2017-53ae-a0d1-64c772d0dcaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-70666" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$\n- **II.** The function is zero at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091 :topic/id #uuid "d9b41e19-22fc-5fad-93ae-b8f50010d70b" :topic/math-academy-id 3557 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991d9c5f-a832-550c-b508-1bc99acc792d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438496} {:answer/id #uuid "699ada80-0b45-5f12-a290-7e8d352f34e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "699ada80-0b45-5f12-a290-7e8d352f34e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438497} :answer-field/id #uuid "70665897-25d9-5fb8-b277-0ed7bc737d42" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66266660-a17d-5cab-9611-596953bfded0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438498} {:answer/id #uuid "529ad213-185b-543a-be0e-63b5e783c340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "529ad213-185b-543a-be0e-63b5e783c340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438499} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9a569f-7beb-55df-b6ed-b7c76b589ecb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9326e664-12a0-57da-b2ff-7159b17d534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438500} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfbb402-00a5-5543-8bc2-4d82370d544c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9326e664-12a0-57da-b2ff-7159b17d534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438500} :answer-field/id #uuid "39ce8d5b-318c-5474-9063-3a51adf37c70" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24b90149-221d-555e-91aa-b1d1cb7cb1c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70667" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$\n\n- **II.** The function has a minimum value at $x=-\\pi .$\n\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The $y$-intercepts of the function is $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function at $x=-\\pi $ has a minimum value.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050427 :topic/id #uuid "48167c86-51da-525c-908a-de3945756954" :topic/math-academy-id 3566 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4111f59a-4b7c-5386-b33f-c50f28c6b443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467806} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8877fa-dbdd-5cc9-920f-2f627ad68b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a8877fa-dbdd-5cc9-920f-2f627ad68b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467807} :answer-field/id #uuid "584dfcf7-c414-5c45-a5d2-c3f57b7c501d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468624} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a62cd36-3671-5aea-909d-1e1fbba55da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467808} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1baf72-e23c-5b90-89c0-467c8a2f799c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a62cd36-3671-5aea-909d-1e1fbba55da0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467808} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a36ebcb-12e9-5824-809d-5c01b37f2b30" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a53073c-9e3e-5db0-80fa-1486b957c632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467810} {:answer/id #uuid "ca319a17-4107-55f9-bf22-cfeb8644f794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca319a17-4107-55f9-bf22-cfeb8644f794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467811} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddab15c-2977-5c7e-aeed-f38132f57ba4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a752d35-73b8-55ea-bb50-4d11f60be65b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70669" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nI. The function has no minimum value. $$\n\nII. $x=-4\\pi $ is in the domain of the function. $$\n\nIII. $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](images/8b/8bc549c68a3bc5b7989ac1835e4bb58183066c7797264b8cccd4f3fd2c895056.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has no minimum or maximum value. $$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $n\\pi $ for any integer $n$, thus it is not defined for $x=-4\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The zeros of $y=cot⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n.$ Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050064 :topic/id #uuid "2a546664-10ba-55b4-ae58-ccb5dd16dca0" :topic/math-academy-id 1483 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "619a4c51-2e05-537d-92f8-05b27adc0576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467812} {:answer/id #uuid "b91d959d-53f8-55db-a51e-4ff6ad7ddc62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "619a4c51-2e05-537d-92f8-05b27adc0576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467812} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdac921-475b-5331-a99d-ec7b6d2ed4c0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468627} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f35e836d-9bb8-578a-a543-2f4893a1ac7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467814} {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ae2b-5562-5a17-b362-7dd84e0030a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb49ae2b-5562-5a17-b362-7dd84e0030a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467815} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfdd3471-0795-5b0b-9ab3-357659c59d0f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7240a062-fdde-5f4a-b323-b6fe3a7554d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467816} {:answer/id #uuid "0d23fd2f-ce53-5110-991d-3c8e82483cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7240a062-fdde-5f4a-b323-b6fe3a7554d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467816} :answer-field/id #uuid "67a4358a-90d6-55fb-8b57-f1e67df2bf37" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc9d880f-4b58-5f10-97af-057cfca9838a" :question/math-academy-id "q-70714" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n- **II.** $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af0b18ca-54a2-5a24-a670-faa311096abc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048794 :topic/id #uuid "bf6b1d4a-a2a5-5f59-9697-5ed210454e3e" :topic/math-academy-id 1486 :topic/title "Graphing the Inverse Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10156616-a9f7-5c47-aa77-4797186d49b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467818} {:answer/id #uuid "27d415f8-955c-56ec-94a5-840b1e90a20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186