on/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a65633b2-f520-54e4-8125-2639c369820d" :question/math-academy-id "q-70778" :question/problem "Which of the following values lies in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $-100$\n- **II.** $-3$\n- **III.** $1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/68/6860bcf04c508b0abe795b9e1699163ac9495818f6427b338ac6bbe17774b2d8.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, all the given values are in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048614 :topic/id #uuid "aedeae90-38bd-5345-9896-abb52aad6dc6" :topic/math-academy-id 2002 :topic/title "Point Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd64c57e-db4c-58c2-9c0a-6fb1e52a8dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467836} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8068b5-f3a3-5dc6-a0ec-cecb527ccb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d8068b5-f3a3-5dc6-a0ec-cecb527ccb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467837} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2422695-230f-5927-9490-102b7e7aad51" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8baeab37-9b1a-57ad-b7b9-83f94da0b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467838} {:answer/id #uuid "38e2dab8-9fb9-5e67-a816-3499bc06a78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8baeab37-9b1a-57ad-b7b9-83f94da0b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467838} :answer-field/id #uuid "7db0f81d-fea3-51ed-b360-51d8b22165a7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5f7ff8-b409-5399-af3b-b0798c72be3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467840} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a5569-d89a-528c-8eda-f01b3b4a0dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a5569-d89a-528c-8eda-f01b3b4a0dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467841} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f8893a-0805-523d-a0fc-3f3104e0d117" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d44ff842-4620-550a-bab6-87cb0a1ac002" :question/math-academy-id "q-71179" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}3x, & x\\ne 4 \\\\ 13, & x=4,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}g(x)$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=g(4)$\n- **III.** $g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(4)=13$ exists$\\,\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{-}}3x=12, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{4}^{+}}3x=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement I is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=12.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)=12,$ while the value of the function is $g(4)=13.$ So, statement II is false and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 4}g(x)\\ne g(4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSince the third condition failed, the function has a removable discontinuity at $x=4,$ and statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048614 :topic/id #uuid "aedeae90-38bd-5345-9896-abb52aad6dc6" :topic/math-academy-id 2002 :topic/title "Point Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33320f01-0cd9-5584-907b-111c2b4618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451501} {:answer/id #uuid "f0914a41-9926-57c2-b640-64e281ead5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0914a41-9926-57c2-b640-64e281ead5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451502} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c990e01-c40c-5da0-8fc4-0a6f039e9d0a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452598} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da9719ef-4224-52d2-9b65-6f8a550d673b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451503} {:answer/id #uuid "af90cee8-740f-5bac-a3e9-97fe948acd5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da9719ef-4224-52d2-9b65-6f8a550d673b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451503} :answer-field/id #uuid "4df650f8-a145-5f16-bbc5-ce42f328ee7e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452599} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f11098-ffae-5d4e-8926-4d749bc054bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451505} {:answer/id #uuid "7e11fba0-bfb2-52ec-a2c1-58f682f5fb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10f11098-ffae-5d4e-8926-4d749bc054bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451505} :answer-field/id #uuid "77d5729b-417b-567c-afdd-26291eaeb1dc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b1ad50f-eeb7-5cca-b60f-fb6418344feb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71180" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}4x, & x<2 \\\\ 4, & x=2 \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x>2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements is true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(2)$ exists\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $f(2)=4$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true.\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}(4x)=8, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}{x}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that statement II is false and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x).\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSince the second condition failed, $x=2$ is not a removable discontinuity. So, statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b5337a-3e06-5fca-8dee-9ccb9bb3e791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467842} {:answer/id #uuid "ca10f725-532e-52f8-b216-80660df1aff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97b5337a-3e06-5fca-8dee-9ccb9bb3e791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467842} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f26b394-09a9-58cd-8127-d23fbca6af8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "572c0f09-8cda-57e4-84ee-e9bf11b0969a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467844} {:answer/id #uuid "3debfd10-6252-58a8-80d0-0fe4ad6b3d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3debfd10-6252-58a8-80d0-0fe4ad6b3d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467845} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b044d1-ec5c-5118-ba8c-99f2a5e9c147" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d92d5ae0-bdbf-5aac-a192-d4634abd4820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467846} {:answer/id #uuid "80aced54-71e3-53cc-8d38-ae55e211374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80aced54-71e3-53cc-8d38-ae55e211374c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467847} :answer-field/id #uuid "7551102b-2721-527c-a9e6-1c6948d2bf34" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e04ff7ee-ed94-5861-b7e8-a3f79254490c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71391" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}}$, clear the denominator in $f(x,y)=c$ and classify the resulting conic equation in the entire $xy$-plane, including points excluded from the function's domain. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=3$ gives a hyperbola\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- **III.** $c=1$ gives a circle" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4}{{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}-4 & =c{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(3-c){y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=3$ then the level curves are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},$ which consists of two vertical lines.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}=4,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ which is a circle.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"} :activity/title "Level Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529572} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530562}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049882 :topic/id #uuid "1ad374f3-e4f4-5dcc-ab6d-d6aed0790f3a" :topic/math-academy-id 1900 :topic/title "Level Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0a2c4b-1d93-5837-bae6-4a3c28e16089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answ