#uuid "eee8ce7b-fa85-591c-9077-2c14699fa270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451559} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2acbd3-d83c-5748-a2a5-8bf95a39efe3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8aec4565-777c-5fd0-95ff-9f5ced653b55" :question/math-academy-id "q-71879" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\n- **II.** $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n\n- **III.** $A={B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $A\\ne {B}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049548 :topic/id #uuid "fe796bc3-3471-557c-9aa6-b1f458fd2aba" :topic/math-academy-id 864 :topic/title "Inverses of 2x2 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd7bbbf-6e0c-51c5-a9fa-fc0f2bf1d945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467896} {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afb67d1-8168-5df5-930f-8190b07edc62" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fa4bf8-f217-5274-8dab-28c162bb278d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467898} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00bd3e1-111e-5780-871b-467da013e81a" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} {:answer/id #uuid "906cb48c-7d29-5136-a248-2c29457a1fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c5cafc-4559-5564-a3f4-1bb51c7edb62" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6118feb2-c751-599a-b3b9-c8c760c49b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71934" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,S=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049548 :topic/id #uuid "fe796bc3-3471-557c-9aa6-b1f458fd2aba" :topic/math-academy-id 864 :topic/title "Inverses of 2x2 Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04e9358-9109-5802-a83d-c003136f6776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467902} {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b39826b-4d43-597b-b35d-5dd3a91ceaf8" :answer-field/key "X" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6c71b-66a8-52d7-88ab-87e3a0607923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f838e05-1a03-57ee-8f9c-10a9e960bcdd" :answer-field/key "Y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62048c-e540-5983-8cbf-aabcf18ff59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2386ffd6-0069-5a17-ae65-0bf5f760c977" :answer-field/key "Z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f09c20fa-fbe3-5a9f-8218-d2a4dd2af13c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d090462-a031-5f96-ac13-90dac882edab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points Where Partial Derivatives Exist" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53636330-9403-5db0-9d17-5dda7fa6783b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451561} {:answer/id #uuid "845ef4ab-3d2a-5524-947f-6cbe1fb7da82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53636330-9403-5db0-9d17-5dda7fa6783b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451561} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f9e12b-29cf-59f8-bf91-cc9a2f919c92" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7b41f94-5879-57a9-a336-092f8f1aede9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451563} {:answer/id #uuid "d65c989f-2d09-5160-b064-ed15ba040057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d65c989f-2d09-5160-b064-ed15ba040057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451564} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa8ff5f-ebba-5ee9-a165-1c4d49347c97" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5f6a07-7680-53e1-ae55-7331a6a7e9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451565} {:answer/id #uuid "c818b116-0775-5d48-9343-c6660016175b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c818b116-0775-5d48-9343-c6660016175b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451566} :answer-field/id #uuid "45930e95-82c6-577a-8b28-a081c55cca47" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452630}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ada5bc24-8a74-58e6-b57b-4b21dfa8df4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72022" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy(z-1))?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The partial derivative with respect to $z$ is defined at $(3,2,1)$\n\n- **II.** ${f}_{y}(1,1,2)$ is defined\n\n- **III.** ${f}_{x}(1,2,3)$ is defined" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot y(z-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot x(z-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot xy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{z-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.  \n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(3,2,1)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(3,2,1)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot 2\\cdot (1-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0),\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.\n\n- Statement II is true. If we substitute $(1,1,2)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,1,2)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot (2-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,1,2) & =\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we substitute $(1,2,3)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 2\\cdot (3-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4),\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,2,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,2,3) & =\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III  only'." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048877 :topic/id #uuid "c8e11bf4-259c-5464-94a3-b5c5d6409c00" :topic/math-academy-id 1932 :topic/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions"} :activity/title "Partial Differentiability of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426702} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426722}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28e2c148-6ee6-5f8c-9b2b-442fe96cf085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467920} {:answer/id #uuid "90143807-a74a-57ee-aa16-a1ee057a16c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90143807-a74a-57ee-aa16-a1ee057a16c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467921} :answer-field/id #uuid "2de9075c-99a1-540e-b78d-991060565cb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8488a4b-f9b2-5a2f-aeff-132fefe2716f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467922} {:answer/id #uuid "1a62f2dd-5c52-5ce6-8102-f840944d8ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a62f2dd-5c52-5ce6-8102-f840944d8ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467923} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5389031-03cb-5727-b801-66a146d9f193" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b7c356-4e59-589f-9d6a-565ed0873aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467924} {:answer/id #uuid "58cf1eb8-5878-59da-b070-f3f00fcdcb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b7c356-4e59-589f-9d6a-565ed0873aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467924} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb366d99-7744-5bfb-8897-cc8aae3154da" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bcd8034-22f3-5298-b8d3-b69cdcbc84fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-72185" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/09/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"} :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429961} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429977} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"} :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446081} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446090}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb3d1e7-cf6a-54b2-a095-b9fdc68a8d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467926} {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927} :answer-field/id #uuid "368ddd66-9d80-586f-9e2a-9ab70f075343" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} {:answer/id #uuid "7d445f31-2d12-5062-a2a4-99e2b64c0491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edea166-3bfd-535f-b98e-b624be2d49a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} {:answer/id #uuid "1541c926-bd73-5e47-854d-d4e15738f59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} :answer-field/id #uuid "88bc4663-71c0-5111-9c92-a5bd0ddc37dc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f581ab20-43e5-59a8-ac58-914378a7361e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72186" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/76/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"} :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406975} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406986}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4ef645-0e9e-59ca-9ead-4e534938e7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae03209-445f-57ef-a7d8-bf499239612a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} {:answer/id #uuid "652141fa-413d-505f-be84-3dff8c027c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a093da-8121-5419-baa0-42398a34c5c0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c7e8b2-4b4c-577e-a27a-0aa07ff9fbc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467936} {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7660e82-ac96-5396-b514-daa03b2886a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b03842bf-e94f-5526-903d-de5a2a3bccca" :question/math-academy-id "q-72187" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/28/28290c5530efd27a979f4284481ca7e0384342d7d426dde0ab36894a0d77a166.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/30/3007cffb725faee44d2a06ad077eec630791b1a94c373a323f62d0d721c87207.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/38/383f88668435556d3a856cf852caf548b1f1bf3a90d50f9d85d7968188984804.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050822 :topic/id #uuid "6961ffb7-2e37-5f54-ac39-0331f4517bbc" :topic/math-academy-id 1979 :topic/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space"} :activity/title "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429961} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186429980}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049511 :topic/id #uuid "fabe76f4-9f30-5b59-b906-f5fa71cfb89f" :topic/math-academy-id 1940 :topic/title "Tangent Lines to Level Curves"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c870de58-6cf8-5f55-bffc-f699bc46f20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439921} {:answer/id #uuid "4e20dcfd-74b5-58d8-ade3-1b14c1ebc0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e20dcfd-74b5-58d8-ade3-1b14c1ebc0f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045