following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050657 :topic/id #uuid "5cf444d7-d014-59c7-b47c-21b442662b58" :topic/math-academy-id 474 :topic/title "Left and Right Continuity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fb1b728-e5c1-56d0-a773-6a13b86c144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467968} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3e086a-3eee-5014-bba7-217442e99470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fb1b728-e5c1-56d0-a773-6a13b86c144a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467968} :answer-field/id #uuid "5010ced0-6c65-57ca-86ab-3156cee7409a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468705} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b93087-ad7b-53c4-b3da-e44b9829803b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467970} {:answer/id #uuid "e772286c-b6b9-5b76-afdf-c7a1d919f850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e772286c-b6b9-5b76-afdf-c7a1d919f850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467971} :answer-field/id #uuid "59560ccb-ca91-5b45-807c-a046f0c20497" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068e637a-e3be-5f92-a484-ea2d9e3dc524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467972} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ebd06a-49a6-522d-8839-e499931d4990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "068e637a-e3be-5f92-a484-ea2d9e3dc524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467972} :answer-field/id #uuid "e764c6f9-b95b-5630-b381-cb9920f27ccc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79464211-37d1-5cac-b164-284bb9d9308a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73105" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad3fb8a0cce2a6dac706d7876aca0a2339fe49c05cb7aa6ae54de86735ceafab.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. The function is left-continuous at $x=3$\n\nII. The function is right-continuous at $x=3$\n\nIII. The function is continuous at $x=3$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=3,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=3,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuit