ning Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid "9d6972e8-70d1-541f-8fd7-7896e8369046" :topic/math-academy-id 1691 :topic/title "Continuity and Differentiability of Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f5c37c5-570d-5441-8e4b-5c969f7aae16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467986} {:answer/id #uuid "3f44968a-7e7f-5529-bb8e-055b55185a66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f5c37c5-570d-5441-8e4b-5c969f7aae16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467986} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa688bb3-f88c-504d-b8e2-9e62938244b9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd45cad1-5bbc-5a54-813a-2150c50e608c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467988} {:answer/id #uuid "3626cf57-a93b-5d4f-b2f3-f442b51235b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3626cf57-a93b-5d4f-b2f3-f442b51235b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467989} :answer-field/id #uuid "bedec394-1b8f-5161-b4fe-464bf879a7cc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69b9b7fc-937d-5985-aacd-223b0dae4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467990} {:answer/id #uuid "805aab3d-23ee-5832-aa96-f6a2647f200c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69b9b7fc-937d-5985-aacd-223b0dae4540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467990} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c8bfe6-070f-588c-b0e6-8c36f67484f7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa88d46b-d2ce-5164-bbed-10d691e29ef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-73250" :question/problem "![](images/a8/a8a70a2f28585b63d2a083b42eb6ad54bfb581b5f13c699a3bc3c8d836afaee8.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The function is continuous at $x=1$\n\nII. The function is continuous at $x=0$\n\nIII. The function is differentiable at $x=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function $f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0$ and so it is not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048420 :topic/id #uuid