is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,5]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $\\sqrt[4]{x}$ is not defined anywhere in the subinterval $[-1,0).$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The intervals $[0,2]$ and $[2,5]$ are closed, and the function is continuous on each of these intervals Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable on each $[0,2]$  and $[2,5].$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"} :activity/title "The Extreme Value Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508384} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509047}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcf8e99e-c1c8-5630-a964-1f28b52afe71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468016} {:answer/id #uuid "154986cd-aed3-511c-a47f-bf8766f5ad6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcf8e99e-c1c8-5630-a964-1f28b52afe71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1