84" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}?$    \n\nI. $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$\n\nII. $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n\nIII. $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$  is closed, but the function is not defined on a part of the interval because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$    is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$ is  closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"} :activity/title "The Extreme Value Theorem" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508384} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509003}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid 