#uuid "fec715a9-1922-5be7-9528-532f2fa723ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468032} :answer-field/id #uuid "7770570e-24c3-51a1-8910-85b4d1c8c7d9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e05c6d3d-29e1-53ab-9c70-1ad2b27199a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-73486" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{x})?$   \n- **I.** $[\\frac{1}{2},1]$\n- **II.** $[0,\\frac{1}{4})$\n- **III.** $[0,1]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[\\frac{1}{2},1]$   is closed, and the function is continuous on $[\\frac{1}{2},1].$   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{1}{4})$  is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=0.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bd74156-928d-5b74-aebc-4099a1b5eafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468034} {:answer/id #uuid "2c06241b-b19c-5161-aaf1-8c7f6a5ba49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bd74156-928d-5b74-aebc-4099a1b5eafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468034} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a215495-71de-5c81-81e9-7523fa7d2d25" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e95fe8db-c741-525c-8be8-9578b9cc090a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468036} {:answer/id #uuid "d3905a03-7cdb-5195-9898-756d1b92d7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e95fe8db-c741-525c-8be8-9578b9cc090a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468036} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c178678-6b88-55af-8ba9-d0a5673f613d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d5dba3-d569-56a0-b16d-9080ac5b9b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468038} {:answer/id #uuid "a4408f9f-a654-5bb2-a53a-a7de5b537763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4408f9f-a654-5bb2-a53a-a7de5b537763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468039} :answer-field/id #uuid "35d5507b-e5da-59d1-9711-6d152ebf51ee" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96d14ec6-ae06-5360-8ddd-d401dbb48508" :question/math-academy-id "q-73487" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\frac{x}{{2}^{x}-1}?$    \n\nI. $[0,1]$\n\nII. $[0,1)$\n\nIII. $[-2,-1]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=0$ (it makes zero the denominator).   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval  $[0,1)$   is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,-1]$    is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,-1].$   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d52bbf-27b3-5866-b828-58197f11fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468040} {:answer/id #uuid "c05f5724-e978-5eea-b92e-be4ff7cc5a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d52bbf-27b3-5866-b828-58197f11fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468040} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc14219f-7f18-5ba0-9fb0-e04cfae28cad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5693a553-a140-59da-b649-fed8ae8eea18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468042} {:answer/id #uuid "5d98483c-577a-5658-83b7-11401637261c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d98483c-577a-5658-83b7-11401637261c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468043} :answer-field/id #uuid "08342a0b-3ffb-5b86-b7e3-32a2e2c374fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6533366-2a36-568d-b35d-24894d19e704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468044} {:answer/id #uuid "96549b46-bd6d-576f-b03c-61ff8c2c2d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6533366-2a36-568d-b35d-24894d19e704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468044} :answer-field/id #uuid "b266eb0d-67ee-5d2a-919e-0f751c92ae28" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b9b884e-eb8a-59c7-aa31-49f0025fb47f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73495" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ -1, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n\nI. $[-1,1]$\n\nII. $[\\frac{1}{2},1]$\n\nIII. $[-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- First, consider $[-1,1].$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}({2}^{-x})={2}^{0}=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-1)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=0$ are not the same. Hence, $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=0.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[-1,1],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\n- Now, consider the interval $[\\frac{1}{2},1].$ In this interval, $f(x)={2}^{-x}$ and so $f(x)$ is continuous on $[\\frac{1}{2},1].$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, the interval $[-1,0)$, is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable in this case.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341991 