:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6d9a215-990f-586e-ad1c-3e2aebcf2b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468116} :answer-field/id #uuid "a971bb90-3bc7-54d6-93ec-562b99c29957" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34143660-ecfa-5585-b65e-76b215171706" :question/math-academy-id "q-75123" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $C?$\n- **I.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $C,$ we write $C=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nC=\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{L}\\cdot \\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}^{U}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix. \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry above the main diagonal. \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as it has an entry not equal to $1$ on the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345092 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048920 :topic/id #uuid "cc887b1d-8841-507d-a99b-b7888c08a675" :topic/math-academy-id 1728 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85e64603-bb6e-5b0f-a72d-80a8ccc3450d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468118} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5f4f63-4be8-5a5b-b8cd-fa7559af4fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85e64603-bb6e-5b0f-a72d-80a8ccc3450d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468118} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1db1d1e-60e6-5396-8aa1-ee91b508535f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2a0153d-23de-5108-888f-f2b222f9131f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468120} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd47bee-3079-5cc3-a48e-29d195deb027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cd47bee-3079-5cc3-a48e-29d195deb027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468121} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4c80179-cb50-56e3-9723-38b39e5ea82c" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83fa1bed-27f2-56b2-bedb-00ae85826918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468122} {:answer/id #uuid "58093b55-be97-532c-ab81-3f3b5e4b6b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83fa1bed-27f2-56b2-bedb-00ae85826918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468122} :answer-field/id #uuid "046de83c-fd46-54bf-b6be-3214402a6cb6" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21485ec9-747a-5129-ba2c-794c570827bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-75496" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048920 :topic/id #uuid "cc887b1d-8841-507d-a99b-b7888c08a675" :topic/math-academy-id 1728 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaf41b36-30bd-512a-957e-7a79e4183513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468124} {:answer/id #uuid "9454a215-809e-5191-9a6a-ef7b9461b589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaf41b36-30bd-512a-957e-7a79e4183513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468124} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a970b3f-aba4-558d-96f5-bdc7558d6367" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "772df56f-6ebc-5441-a57c-8fa34430e871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468126} {:answer/id #uuid "e901e9d8-5277-5853-a8d8-aa947bc28455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "772df56f-6ebc-5441-a57c-8fa34430e871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468126} :answer-field/id #uuid "b66a9f09-6423-5df3-a9e6-c1ecb588dfbd" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "884da85b-8267-58aa-bc44-864b1dfae649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468128} {:answer/id #uuid "311831d9-638e-53b5-81bc-b745969c5e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "311831d9-638e-53b5-81bc-b745969c5e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468129} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5aef87e-7739-5996-90df-061493f26c42" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9438fd33-674b-505b-988d-ed78456eace8" :question/math-academy-id "q-75503" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048920 :topic/id #uuid "cc887b1d-8841-507d-a99b-b7888c08a675" :topic/math-academy-id 1728 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1c880af-d051-51c9-ab73-b924750b1cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218646813