468134} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6d0674-f6ff-5e1f-b038-2070323a0549" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8b28abc-ffbd-5f2b-b51a-6be08eb05498" :question/math-academy-id "q-75508" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" 