d{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3917c546-1a71-5b69-95fa-031bd8a95f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468148} {:answer/id #uuid "685efbb1-a98a-5e24-81fb-c69c96152f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218