culty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c2c6cc4-6d0f-5ca4-bd69-989208f699b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-78132" :question/problem "![](images/89/890e7eaf519a65ca19d4a90b604e7d7a8ab7054635296c4b08f000546f23b545.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-2$\n\n- **II.** $x=1$\n\n- **III.** $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $-2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ Since there is a jump at $x=1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous $x=3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of  $x=3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and III only\".\n\n![](images/7c/7c96c401ddae0049859fd5608cb08c6ce9ae8a2e6c3db69d7d4b379b3824094e.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68350e0d-84ca-5b50-b05a-1bca3ceea40f" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 3x3 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049684 :topic/id #uuid "0aa448d3-ff23-589f-85d0-370c4ca9baa8" :topic/math-academy-id 1732 :topic/title "Finding the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using Row Operations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c45ee0d5-9308-555e-8655-27b49940846a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468220} {:answer/id #uuid "01fd75aa-adb0-55a4-a4a6-505837749218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45ee0d5-9308-555e-8655-27b49940846a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468220} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8821c63-a7c5-5ece-9e8b-2cf346755fea" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79c8137b-cfe0-5491-acb8-08e31e6b36a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468222} {:answer/id #uuid "54d834f8-d01e-5030-b6db-31e199e73c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54d834f8-d01e-5030-b6db-31e199e73c16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468223} :answer-field/id #uuid "5df3bbee-6432-59a0-a00f-c0b239fb51db" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44748425-a40a-50f9-9a5f-8d6b21698bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468224} {:answer/id #uuid "3e68b5b1-8455-51e8-87d7-ba9e6d6c1d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44748425-a40a-50f9-9a5f-8d6b21698bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468224} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5f0085-a29d-5b62-b75a-4b1190f65885" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad44d2b4-38e0-5faa-8080-32a8feda902f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78772" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "662abe6b-b2cd-5ea9-8a2f-ff2dbf3aebcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451669} {:answer/id #uuid "c1699e8e-3c35-5e73-9fca-90eaf3042d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1699e8e-3c35-5e73-9fca-90eaf3042d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451670} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb7ee7c-156b-594e-a8ce-345226739051" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bbfe73b-366e-571e-a31c-31100f9f3e36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451671} {:answer/id #uuid "22ba9e19-e742-59a6-9d92-de445eeeaba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22ba9e19-e742-59a6-9d92-de445eeeaba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451672} :answer-field/id #uuid "467a0d89-a6f8-5efb-a649-e95e37c71ac3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "632e177b-eb1a-5d32-96f7-f7cb3a05bfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451673} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5932ef-fa86-5e75-8a10-ac7fc1d30ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "632e177b-eb1a-5d32-96f7-f7cb3a05bfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451673} :answer-field/id #uuid "52876036-7563-5e0e-b371-a31bda5802db" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d2cfdcc8-d9c8-57ce-9941-2dd5f51fdf5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78960" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=({x}^{2}-6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi )$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi )$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-({x}^{2}-6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =(2-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =(2-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & >0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this inequality by considering the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ over the interval $[0,\\pi ].$\n\n![](images/41/410e0af2ed20a065c27da5edaf0095dfd22c8a37a92e3d8fbaeece629cefa278.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0$ when $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\pi .$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x>0,$ which has the solution $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105710 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff7c597d-d4a4-5567-add6-eac77475b0d6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Are Neither Local Minima nor Local Maxima" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048478 :topic/id #uuid "a2bb3232-296a-5d16-b145-1ee30beae8b3" :topic/math-academy-id 1360 :topic/title "Using the First Derivative Test to Classify Local Extrema"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7b8ef8d-4b75-5b2f-b2a7-b29ce853eea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451675} {:answer/id #uuid "253b55e7-003d-5b34-b611-76a8f0565050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "253b55e7-003d-5b34-b611-76a8f0565050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451676} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac2f9cd3-5d24-5653-b0ec-c55f214668e8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7926eb6-871e-525f-a939-d18e5dc12fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451677} {:answer/id #uuid "688d6d0d-ed2e-59c7-83d5-55c143400e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "688d6d0d-ed2e-59c7-83d5-55c143400e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451678} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a7b3503-e057-5b77-8dfa-3940176d78ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ae074a5-93d7-5984-adda-364b3e9e3ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451679} {:answer/id #uuid "e52df1a2-5e12-5892-af31-9eccbb37e5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ae074a5-93d7-5984-adda-364b3e9e3ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451679} :answer-field/id #uuid "796f6a55-6846-5e2e-ae5b-61f10223798e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4e347bc5-2d93-561c-bcc0-048e510bad1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79001" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x)=2+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ is a local maximum\n- **II.** $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum\n- **III.** $x=0$ is a local minimum" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the stationary points. Differentiating $f(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}=2{x}^{2}(3-2x).\n$$\n\nAnd now find the stationary points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}(3-2x)=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=0,\\,\\frac{3}{2}.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-1,1,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =2(-1)^{2}(3-2(-1))=10>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(1) & =2(1)^{2}(3-2(1))=2>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =2(2)^{2}(3-2(2))=-8<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,0)$ | $0$ | $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $(\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-1$ |  | $1$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ |  | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=0,$ the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=0$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=\\frac{3}{2}$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da3a19c-bae7-5f63-a92a-8aa2edb12e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468226} {:answer/id #uuid "15a8ee57-8581-51f7-affe-d87ddfbf508c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4da3a19c-bae7-5f63-a92a-8aa2edb12e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468226} :answer-field/id #uuid "44b5749e-c13c-50fb-93b9-69de4485ab3c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb762ba-786d-5da5-837f-acc4923ee13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468228} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0eb5a-dd62-5cfe-80d2-22b8ce295705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4a0eb5a-dd62-5cfe-80d2-22b8ce295705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468229} :answer-field/id #uuid "f89886cf-5411-5d82-abe0-ca1b8f449eb6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6742387-a48f-5ec0-b87b-420fa980f2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468230} {:answer/id #uuid "482654bb-b196-5304-90f8-6b2f88ab2855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6742387-a48f-5ec0-b87b-420fa980f2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468230} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e82116-2782-52b5-8af7-e1a83d25a791" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3b9e269-d2c5-5e09-8e6b-2689345ee964" :question/math-academy-id "q-79039" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+5x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(2,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(2,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,2)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}-12x+5 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & >0\\,⟹\\,x>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the function is concave up on $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $6x-12<0,$ which has the solution $(-\\infty ,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a2aeb0f-ac98-5378-8ff2-051f09938504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451681} {:answer/id #uuid "a82d5b88-aac4-593f-8eaa-6546fd5f9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a82d5b88-aac4-593f-8eaa-6546fd5f9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451682} :answer-field/id #uuid "feca05ea-a39c-5037-b0b7-bd4eba6ca4ff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d86a7bb-971a-5a11-b395-25154adfcf56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451683} {:answer/id #uuid "84c75233-0053-547a-adb1-ad731da53a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84c75233-0053-547a-adb1-ad731da53a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451684} :answer-field/id #uuid "0783c636-2215-523f-9370-29cecfdfff20" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d91e6c7-d5c2-552a-9309-2e2a93f03b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451685} {:answer/id #uuid "005040e5-ae0c-5ac1-be47-97fbb16c8dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d91e6c7-d5c2-552a-9309-2e2a93f03b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451685} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6f4780-8f4a-5138-b9b0-fa13950dcc14" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ff0b214-682b-57ba-8449-74aff3e87403" :question/math-academy-id "q-79040" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-2x$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,2)$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,0)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}-24x=12x(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x(x-2) & >0 \\\\ x(x-2) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this inequality by considering the graph of $y=x(x-2).$\n\n![](images/cb/cb06747b13b36bc1b53f96df8d1345332200ecb8b7728342d7086963b51d86f5.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that $x(x-2)>0$ when $x<0$ and $x>2.$ So the graph is concave up on the intervals  $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $x(x-2)<0,$ which has the solution $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f544782b-2834-5ba1-9e55-1dca65881824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451687} {:answer/id #uuid "29465dc2-f1a7-5d58-a423-5ca5c0e1ffc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29465dc2-f1a7-5d58-a423-5ca5c0e1ffc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451688} :answer-field/id #uuid "d08b562d-4983-5058-9f80-8106be2bad70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3224e2e8-4a51-5bb2-a50a-f5d5b72158f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451689} {:answer/id #uuid "4329381f-e7e5-5396-918f-e2a8fb9d4656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3224e2e8-4a51-5bb2-a50a-f5d5b72158f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451689} :answer-field/id #uuid "04930d4b-7492-52be-9f3d-4806c9ee36ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35837f73-5da3-511b-862d-ea26a5c2ee74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451691} {:answer/id #uuid "0455f902-0466-5f14-bf24-4a73eaa990a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35837f73-5da3-511b-862d-ea26a5c2ee74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451691} :answer-field/id #uuid "27714d34-b2d3-5af9-8b84-ad016200cfeb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8641b3e-61ff-5ab9-ae03-84509bab9465" :question/math-academy-id "q-79041" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-1,1)$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,-1)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12x-4{x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12-12{x}^{2} \\\\  & =12(1-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =12(1+x)(1-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1+x)(1-x) & >0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-1) & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this inequality by considering the graph of $y=(x+1)(x-1).$\n\n![](images/09/09b4b237ec87a63e6de47eea5ed9156febbed0271dd0688c0be1c22a62c50c4e.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that $(x+1)(x-1)<0$ when $-1<x<1.$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(-1,1).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $(x+1)(x-1)>0,$ which has the solutions $(-\\infty ,-1)$ and $(1,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b95a376-c965-5a6e-b6d9-4e1e8d4f5c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451693} {:answer/id #uuid "cb668dfb-1988-546d-aab1-8bc8a3beda74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb668dfb-1988-546d-aab1-8bc8a3beda74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451694} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b73ec4f-9627-554b-a55c-9ff20f5b8455" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "679de6b8-b120-5db2-80f4-5a0aea48074d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451695} {:answer/id #uuid "925b1a7d-5c35-567d-95a8-1c3d38688dd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "679de6b8-b120-5db2-80f4-5a0aea48074d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451695} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dd4ab56-9f7e-581f-9063-2bb731e04f84" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4a9e047-d7d0-56b4-9d3c-9fc93cc4275f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451697} {:answer/id #uuid "0926c6b8-5bfa-57f1-9295-1d8386492262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0926c6b8-5bfa-57f1-9295-1d8386492262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451698} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fac72e1-40b8-5fbc-97d2-033b133c2be5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e3ee0d0-3aa0-549f-96be-2f320dd749a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-79045" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=6+{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(2,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(2,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,2)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & >0\\,⟹\\,x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the function is concave up on $(-\\infty ,2).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $2-x<0,$ which has the solution $(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050120 :topic/id #uuid "2e9764be-8ae2-5f34-ba40-eb17adf36f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3846 :topic/title "Relating Concavity to the Second Derivative"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1adde2ed-c4f7-5734-8c3f-eb67f9abdd04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468232} {:answer/id #uuid "997a6115-1fcd-5a23-ab8c-6b095c28db63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "997a6115-1fcd-5a23-ab8c-6b095c28db63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468233} :answer-field/id #uuid "214f072a-2b9b-5c54-8a48-75f1d2077938" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb63a92f-25d6-5b16-b9d4-e7f3ef16b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468234} {:answer/id #uuid "7109cabe-f6be-5136-8e97-e984fddf18b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb63a92f-25d6-5b16-b9d4-e7f3ef16b277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468234} :answer-field/id #uuid "e374045c-c62c-5a82-a5a3-2c2566468094" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e20cf84-d315-5c52-b67d-452dbac3a614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468236} {:answer/id #uuid "d0adc2dc-4f6c-5175-bfd1-9ddc095f41b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e20cf84-d315-5c52-b67d-452dbac3a614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468236} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac889658-7863-5a11-99e1-66be48a3a419" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d60b7843-0bd3-5e4e-8b85-becdd36b22ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-79047" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2+3x-{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3+{e}^{-x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{-x}>0$ for every real value of $x,$ it follows that $-{e}^{-x}<0$ for every real value of $x.$ Therefore, ${f}^{″}(x)$ is never positive, so there are no intervals where $f(x)$ is concave up.\n\nSince ${f}^{″}(x)<0$ for every real value of $x,$ the function is concave down on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125 :topic/id #uuid "dcaddd67-a2eb-5a06-88ab-be47014dbd14" :topic/math-academy-id 863 :topic/title "Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e187316-ca4b-5005-8c16-92779ad4da33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451699} {:answer/id #uuid "4d689f5f-05dd-57b7-954c-3d17ae60ca4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d689f5f-05dd-57b7-954c-3d17ae60ca4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451700} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b27b52-6dbe-5ddb-bbef-45bd0b09c851" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b0f342-4a40-5b35-b50c-a9da5c348610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451701} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac73bcb-c0d1-5514-8e54-fcb26aa4a0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b0f342-4a40-5b35-b50c-a9da5c348610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451701} :answer-field/id #uuid "494ea162-0b29-5250-b36b-ebe80cf3f333" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0243a92-3db2-5dbe-be64-260ae8db1223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451703} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc97d95-3773-50f3-8780-9c6e598ff7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc97d95-3773-50f3-8780-9c6e598ff7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451704} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ab34c7-38e4-50f8-9406-f9655142cf5a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3b65f93-463c-54d1-85ca-57a9749888f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-7905" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\n- **II.** $AE=EA={I}_{3}$\n\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AE=EA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AE & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ -10 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125 :topic/id #uuid "dcaddd67-a2eb-5a06-88ab-be47014dbd14" :topic/math-academy-id 863 :topic/title "Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dd76501-c60c-5bce-9ffc-b4d3b28fd3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451705} {:answer/id #uuid "51753a09-2255-5845-8d27-ebe20a632dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2dd76501-c60c-5bce-9ffc-b4d3b28fd3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451705} :answer-field/id #uuid "03948866-0b24-52c3-8253-b493c8d73592" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db9de1c-b97f-569b-b5d7-ee1b92b0f720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451707} {:answer/id #uuid "fd503f10-de25-5ab0-bb92-dd3358bee9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd503f10-de25-5ab0-bb92-dd3358bee9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451708} :answer-field/id #uuid "59605bbd-4695-50af-b923-5d960bdaa68e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25defdb9-192b-5a27-8848-1256ba3b6345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451709} {:answer/id #uuid "1721e2cd-1c3a-5cf8-a293-7ba1b2112a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1721e2cd-1c3a-5cf8-a293-7ba1b2112a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451710} :answer-field/id #uuid "88140b3a-d029-5345-baf0-7023275454a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a09e0ac-b938-5176-9b09-5c3e47da17ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-7907" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n- **II.** $BD=DB={I}_{3}$\n- **III.** $D={B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{15} & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Note, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125 :topic/id #uuid "dcaddd67-a2eb-5a06-88ab-be47014dbd14" :topic/math-academy-id 863 :topic/title "Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df2e0d17-fa3f-5143-a321-2a068c4e955c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/iden