186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8289966f-f636-5804-9edf-c054d1b5acd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-79457" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers lie in the second quadrant in the corresponding Argand diagram?\n- **I.** $-2-2\\text{i}$\n- **II.** $-2+\\text{i}$\n- **III.** $-1+2\\text{i}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The complex number $-2-2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=-2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,-2)$, which lies in the third quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-2+\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-2$ and the imaginary part $y=1.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-2,1)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n- The complex number $-1+2\\text{i}$ has the real part $x=-1$ and the imaginary part $y=2.$ So, it corresponds to the point $(-1,2)$, which lies in the second quadrant.\n\n![](images/9f/9f2e7234ba52d14098e0ecfc9695181b425764c110995b76b4b0efddf206252c.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b612ef-ce7f-5783-848d-d8ef210c9f47" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Argand Diagram Corresponding to a Complex Number" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050191 :topic/id #uuid "35093636-213e-50dc-8f50-148c780d5517" :topic/math-academy-id 157 :topic/title "The Complex Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f205a47-e876-5904-9c32-be819d450a78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468256} {:answer/id #uuid "ff48e516-9cb1-5552-9ba7-1f72499e9f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1